const DISPLAY_NAMES={"Manchester City": "Man City", "AFC Bournemouth": "B'mouth", "Nottingham Forest": "Nott'm Forest", "Tottenham Hotspur": "Tottenham", "Newcastle United": "Newcastle", "Crystal Palace": "C. Palace", "Leeds United": "Leeds", "Ipswich Town": "Ipswich", "AS Roma": "Roma", "Rayo Vallecano": "Rayo", "Celta Vigo": "Celta", "Bayer Leverkusen": "Leverkusen", "SC Paderborn 07": "Paderborn", "Borussia M\u00f6nchengladbach": "Gladbach", "Borussia Dortmund": "Dortmund", "Eintracht Frankfurt": "Frankfurt", "TSG Hoffenheim": "Hoffenheim", "SV Elversberg": "Elversberg", "SC Freiburg": "Freiburg", "1. FC Union Berlin": "Union Berlin", "RB Leipzig": "Leipzig", "Schalke 04": "Schalke", "VfB Stuttgart": "Stuttgart", "Paris Saint-Germain": "PSG", "AS Monaco": "Monaco", "AJ Auxerre": "Auxerre", "Queens Park Rangers": "QPR", "Southampton": "S'hampton", "Derby County": "Derby", "Bolton Wanderers": "Bolton", "Birmingham City": "Birmingham", "Lincoln City": "Lincoln", "West Bromwich Albion": "West Brom", "Middlesbrough": "M'boro", "Bristol City": "Bristol City", "West Ham United": "West Ham", "Preston North End": "Preston", "Wolverhampton Wanderers": "Wolves", "Charlton Athletic": "Charlton", "Sheffield United": "Sheff Utd", "Norwich City": "Norwich", "Cardiff City": "Cardiff"};


















Object.assign(E.preview,{"fc-20261123-01": "Brentford return home in tenth place on 14 points, but their last five competitive games brought one win, one draw and three defeats. Beating Nottingham Forest without conceding shows they remain difficult hosts. However, Igor Thiago's suspension and the injuries to Aaron Hickey and Nathan Collins force changes at both ends. Everton are seventh on 16 points and have won their last three games after two defeats. Their away win at Newcastle and subsequent victory over Coventry provide momentum, while Barry's scoring form gives the weakened home defence a specific problem. Brentford's home advantage makes this a demanding assignment, but Everton's improving attack and fuller squad make Everton my selection.", "fc-20261123-02": "Monza need a home response, but four consecutive defeats expose a defence that has not found stability. They are eighteenth on seven points, having followed victory over Cagliari with losses to Torino, Napoli, Bologna and Atalanta. Fiorentina are only fifteenth on nine points, yet their direction is more encouraging: draws with Atalanta and Juventus came either side of an away win over Sassuolo. Vanoli's side have shown they can score away, although conceding in all five of their latest games prevents complete confidence. Pongracic and Parisi remain unavailable, giving Monza an opening. Even so, Fiorentina's improving results offer a stronger basis than Monza's losing run. Fiorentina are my selection.", "fc-20261123-03": "This relegation-zone meeting carries particular weight for Levante, eighteenth on 11 points and only one ahead of nineteenth-placed Elche. Both Levante league wins this season came at home. Their last five competitive games contain two wins, a draw and two defeats, but the cup success over Tarancon required extra time and does not by itself establish a league recovery. Elche lost their latest two matches without scoring, although the away league win at Rayo demonstrates that their home difficulties should not be projected onto their travelling form. Manu Sanchez is available again for Levante, while Marc Aguado remains out for Elche. The visitors' away resilience makes this close, but Levante's home wins over Athletic and Betis give the hosts a narrow attacking case. Levante are my selection.", "fc-20261120-01": "Athletic return to San Mames with three wins, a draw and one defeat in their last five competitive matches. Victories over Getafe and Real Sociedad give the hosts grounds for confidence, while their 16 points put them seventh. Espanyol are 13th on 12 points and have won only one of five, although beating Villarreal and then holding Deportivo without conceding suggests defensive improvement. Athletic should therefore avoid forcing the game and exposing space behind their attacks. Their stronger recent winning record and home advantage nevertheless make Athletic Club my selection.", "fc-20261120-02": "Bayern welcome Vincent Kompany back to the touchline while seeking to strengthen their lead. They have 21 points from nine unbeaten league games and four wins plus a draw in their last five competitive outings. Cologne are 15th on nine points and winless in four league matches, leaving them vulnerable to sustained pressure at the Allianz Arena. Manuel Neuer, Serge Gnabry and Alphonso Davies are among Bayern's absentees, but the hosts have scored 20 goals in four home league games. Jamal Musiala's possible return is encouraging. Bayern's pressing, attacking depth and home dominance make Bayern Munich my selection.", "fc-20261120-03": "This meeting of the bottom two gives Troyes an important home opportunity. They are 17th with eight points after ten matches and remain short of goals, but clean sheets against Toulouse and Le Mans show that defensive organisation can bring results. Le Havre are last on two points, have no league win and have lost all five of their latest competitive matches. Heavy concessions against Marseille and PSG underline the visitors' difficulties. Troyes should build pressure patiently rather than overcommit. Neither side inspires complete confidence, but home advantage and the stronger league record make Troyes my selection.", "fc-20261120-04": "Only three points separate sixth-placed Bielefeld, on 17, from fourth-placed Magdeburg, on 20. The hosts have beaten Braunschweig and Holstein Kiel in successive league games and return home with confidence. Magdeburg's convincing win over St Pauli confirms their attacking danger, but their recent results also include a heavy cup defeat at Bayern. Bielefeld should resist turning this into an uncontrolled exchange and instead protect midfield space. Their consecutive league wins and home advantage make Arminia Bielefeld my selection.", "fc-20261120-05": "Darmstadt need to restore both their scoring threat and defensive stability. They are 17th on nine points and have recently lost to Nuremberg and heavily to Karlsruhe. Heidenheim are seventh on 16 points, although three draws and two defeats in five mean their higher position should not be mistaken for strong form. Scoring twice against Hannover in their latest draw offers encouragement, particularly against an unsettled home defence. This looks close rather than straightforward, but Heidenheim's stronger season record and opportunity to exploit Darmstadt's weaknesses make Heidenheim my selection.", "fc-20261120-06": "Molde's high-scoring matches reveal defensive problems as well as attacking strength. Their latest draw with Sandefjord involved five goals conceded, a vulnerability second-placed Bodo/Glimt can target. Molde have 44 points in fifth, compared with the visitors' 62. Bodo/Glimt have won their last two league matches against Viking and Tromso and also kept Lille scoreless in Europe. Both attacks can open the game up, but the visitors' stronger season-long record and ability to exploit space make Bodo/Glimt my selection.", "fc-20261120-07": "AGF's clean-sheet win over Horsens provides a useful foundation. Eighth on 15 points, the hosts have two wins, two draws and a defeat in five competitive matches, including a goalless European draw with Braga. Lyngby are tenth on 11 points and have lost three of five, most recently failing to score against Silkeborg. Their win over Randers and scoring threat against Nordsjaelland mean AGF must still protect against counters. Better recent defensive control and home advantage make AGF my selection.", "fc-20261120-08": "Cercle Brugge have regained confidence through successive wins over Antwerp and La Louviere, the latter with a clean sheet. Three earlier defeats show that the recovery still needs consolidation. Westerlo's last two games brought heavy concessions against Anderlecht and Charleroi, making defensive repair urgent. Their earlier wins confirm attacking potential, so Cercle should avoid an unnecessarily open match. With improving defensive confidence and home advantage, Cercle Brugge are my selection.", "fc-20261120-09": "Verona's unbeaten five-match run is built on defensive stability. They beat Juve Stabia and Carrarese without conceding before drawing scoreless with Mantova, giving them three consecutive clean sheets. Fifth place on 16 points looks much higher than Cesena's 12th, but only one point separates them. Cesena have recently beaten Empoli and Catanzaro and deserve respect. Verona's ability to protect their goal can nevertheless allow a small number of chances to decide the match. Home advantage and defensive consistency make Hellas Verona my selection.", "fc-20261120-10": "Andorra's home advantage is offset by poor league results. They are 21st on 11 points and have recently lost to Girona, Burgos and Almeria while also conceding twice in a draw with Tenerife. Leganes are 16th on 15 points and remain inconsistent, but have won their last cup match and then beaten Burgos in the league. Their earlier heavy concessions against Valladolid and Albacete prevent a confident defensive assessment. Both sides have weaknesses, yet the visitors' return to winning form makes Leganes my selection.", "fc-20261120-11": "Annecy's stronger league position needs to be weighed against two consecutive heavy league defeats to Montpellier and Boulogne. They are ninth on 16 points, while their cup advancement came on penalties after a drawn match rather than a clear playing-time victory. Clermont are 15th on 11 points and have drawn frequently, but their latest league win over Rodez came with a clean sheet and was followed by a convincing cup win. The hosts' defensive uncertainty and the visitors' recent improvement make Clermont Foot my selection.", "fc-20261120-12": "Guingamp and Rodez both arrive with uneven results and only one point between them: 14 for the hosts in 11th and 13 for the visitors in 13th. Guingamp beat Clermont and Saint-Etienne without conceding before a heavy loss to Dunkerque. Rodez also won twice before losing their latest league and cup matches. Guingamp's cup exit came on penalties and should be distinguished from a playing-time defeat. This is close, but the hosts' recent evidence of clean-sheet wins and home advantage make Guingamp my selection.", "fc-20261120-13": "Metz's league win at Montpellier gives them attacking encouragement despite a subsequent cup defeat. Seventh on 17 points, they can maintain pressure on the upper places. Boulogne are 12th on 13 and have drawn seven of 12 league matches, suggesting they can frustrate opponents. Their clean-sheet win over Annecy was positive, though they also lost in the cup. Metz must stay patient and protect against counters rather than chase an early breakthrough recklessly. Home advantage and their recent league scoring performance make Metz my selection.", "fc-20261120-14": "Nancy's four consecutive league wins provide the strongest platform in this match. Second on 25 points, they kept clean sheets against Laval and Sochaux. Their cup advancement came through a shootout after a draw and should not be counted as a playing-time win, but the league sequence remains impressive. Dijon are sixth on 18 points and have beaten Grenoble and Red Star in their last two league fixtures. They remain a threat, although a cup loss and earlier league defeats show less consistency. Nancy's sustained league form and home advantage make Nancy my selection.", "fc-20261120-15": "Red Star's cup win does not erase four consecutive league defeats. Eighth on 17 points, they have struggled to score while their defence has been under pressure. Pau are fifth on 20 points and beat Guingamp, Grenoble and Metz in successive league matches before losing to Nantes. They responded with a convincing cup win. The hosts may take encouragement from their own cup result, but the visitors have shown more reliable league scoring and winning form. Pau are my selection.", "fc-20261121-01": "City must respond to three successive league defeats. Their five competitive games brought ten goals conceded, while Fulham conceded only three in five and drew with Newcastle last time. Maresca's confirmation that Marc Guehi is available helps the hosts, but patience and defensive balance remain essential. Home advantage and their chance creation give Manchester City a narrow preference.", "fc-20261121-02": "Villa's 4-4 draw at United showed attacking promise and serious defensive problems. They have only one win in five, while Sunderland arrive after beating Chelsea without conceding. The visitors deserve respect, but Villa's attacking response and home advantage give the hosts a cautious preference.", "fc-20261121-03": "Bournemouth have won five competitive games in a row, scoring 13 and conceding two. Forest's win over City is a warning against complacency, but the hosts have the more sustained record. Scott and Kroupi's availability helps Marco Rose, while Forest lack Hudson-Odoi. Bournemouth are the selection.", "fc-20261121-04": "Chelsea need sharper finishing after losing to Sunderland; their last five brought only five goals. Leeds beat Tottenham but scored just three in five themselves. Caicedo is available, although Chelsea retain several absences. A tight contest is likely, with home advantage favouring Chelsea.", "fc-20261121-05": "Both clubs are near the bottom. Coventry scored and conceded nine in five, while Palace scored only three. Thomas Frank's first match may bring a response, but Mateta's suspension and Sarr's injury limit the visitors. Coventry's greater recent attacking output and home advantage earn a narrow preference.", "fc-20261121-06": "Tottenham's defeat at Leeds followed three consecutive wins and should not erase their defensive improvement: only three conceded in five. Ipswich have gone four without a win. Savio and Bergvall are available again, although Tel remains out. Tottenham's stronger balance at home makes them the selection.", "fc-20261121-07": "Newcastle have only one win in five. Arsenal lead with 27 points and conceded only twice in their last five competitive games. Saliba is available again, but Zubimendi and Saka are out. The hosts can make this uncomfortable, yet Arsenal's defensive consistency makes them the selection.", "fc-20261121-08": "Como's loss to Inter ended four straight wins; they still scored 15 in five. Cagliari stopped four defeats by beating Frosinone, but conceded 12 across that five-game run. Como's stronger attacking record and home advantage make them the selection.", "fc-20261121-09": "Lazio remain top on 29 points after drawing with Napoli, with four wins and a draw in five and 14 goals scored. Lecce stopped three defeats by drawing with Torino but remain winless in four. The hosts' consistency and attacking output favour Lazio.", "fc-20261121-10": "Parma have only one win in five and eight league points. Roma beat Sassuolo without conceding and scored 17 in five, although ten conceded show that their defence is not secure. Their greater attacking threat and third-place standing give Roma the preference.", "fc-20261121-11": "Only one point separates these teams, and both are winless in three. Napoli's draw with leaders Lazio was encouraging, although 11 conceded in five remain a concern. Torino have also struggled for consistency. Napoli receive a narrow home preference rather than a strong endorsement.", "fc-20261121-12": "Alaves' six-goal cup win should not erase the four winless matches before it. Deportivo are unbeaten in three and conceded only three in five. With the visitors ninth on 15 points and more defensively reliable, Deportivo receive a cautious preference.", "fc-20261121-13": "Rayo's defeat at Sociedad followed two wins. Valencia's six-goal cup success should be distinguished from their league defeat by Real Madrid and 19th-place position. Rayo have the modest table advantage and play at home, earning a cautious preference.", "fc-20261121-14": "Derby intensity reduces the value of table position alone. Sevilla are winless in two, while Betis have won twice and sit eight points ahead. Betis must avoid the defensive lapses seen in their cup game, but recent consistency gives the visitors the preference.", "fc-20261121-15": "Madrid have won five competitive games in a row, scoring 15, and beat Valencia without conceding. Celta's five-goal cup victory followed four winless matches and came in a different competitive context. Madrid's more sustained record and home advantage make them the selection.", "fc-20261121-16": "Leverkusen ended two defeats by beating Cologne, but 11 conceded in five show continuing defensive risk. Paderborn's draw with Frankfurt merits respect; friendly results are excluded from the competitive assessment. Leverkusen receive a home preference, provided they protect space behind their attacks.", "fc-20261121-17": "Gladbach's friendly win is excluded from the competitive assessment. Their four league points and bottom position contrast with Dortmund's 21 points and unbeaten five-match competitive run. The visitors still concede chances, but Dortmund's more consistent results make them the selection.", "fc-20261121-18": "Both teams have 12 points and conceded five in their last five. Frankfurt are unbeaten in three, while Hoffenheim responded by beating Schalke but remain inconsistent. The margins look small; Frankfurt's recent continuity and home advantage earn a narrow preference.", "fc-20261121-19": "Elversberg remain a credible home opponent but conceded 12 in five. Freiburg have won four in a row and kept a clean sheet against Union. The hosts can score, yet Freiburg's stronger recent balance makes the visitors the selection.", "fc-20261121-20": "Union's seven league points and limited scoring are concerns after their goalless defeat at Wolfsburg. Leipzig's friendly is excluded from the assessment; their fourth place and 18 points provide the stronger competitive basis. Leipzig are preferred, with defensive concentration still essential away from home.", "fc-20261121-21": "Schalke have lost three straight and scored once in five. Stuttgart arrive after a clean-sheet win over Bremen and have three wins in five. Away inconsistency remains a risk, but the hosts' limited scoring makes Stuttgart the preference.", "fc-20261121-22": "Nice have won three straight and scored 12 in five, so this is a real test. PSG have won all five, scoring 18 and conceding three. Both can threaten, but PSG's stronger balance at both ends gives the league leaders the preference.", "fc-20261121-23": "Monaco are unbeaten in two and have the stronger league position. Auxerre have lost twice in a row and conceded 12 in five. The visitors can slow the game, but Monaco's more stable record and home advantage make them the selection.", "fc-20261121-24": "Lille are unbeaten in three after beating Rennes and sit second on 21 points. Lyon are fifth but scored only three in five and lost without scoring at Brest. With chances potentially scarce, Lille's recent stability at home gives them the preference.", "fc-20261121-25": "Both clubs have 13 points, but Lens have lost three straight and conceded 16 in five. Toulouse beat Strasbourg and conceded only five across their last five. The hosts can respond, yet the visitors' defensive balance gives Toulouse a cautious preference.", "fc-20261121-26": "Strasbourg have lost four of five and conceded 12. Brest have won their last two, most recently without conceding against Lyon, and scored 11 while allowing four in five. The visitors' stronger form at both ends makes Brest the selection.", "fc-20261121-27": "Norwich's five-goal win over Bristol City extended a four-match winning run. Cardiff scored five against Burnley but conceded four, illustrating their defensive risk. Norwich's better recent balance and home advantage make them the selection.", "fc-20261121-28": "Millwall have lost their last two, most recently without scoring at West Brom. QPR beat Lincoln and are unbeaten in two, although nine conceded in five reveal defensive risk. Their stronger table position and recent response earn QPR a cautious preference.", "fc-20261121-29": "Southampton's defeat to Preston was poor, but it followed four unbeaten games. Derby ended four winless matches by beating Bolton, yet remain 23rd with ten points and 11 conceded in five. The hosts' stronger overall balance favours Southampton.", "fc-20261121-30": "Portsmouth's loss to Stoke followed four unbeaten matches. Bolton have only one win in five and conceded 11, compared with Portsmouth's five. Home pressure is a factor, but the visitors' stronger defensive continuity makes Portsmouth the selection.", "fc-20261121-31": "Both sides have 29 points and three successive wins. Stoke conceded only two in five; Birmingham scored 11 while conceding three. This is a close contest between strong teams. Birmingham receive only a marginal preference for their greater attacking output.", "fc-20261121-32": "Lincoln have lost three straight. Wrexham drew with Wolves and are unbeaten in two, conceding only five in their last five. The hosts urgently need points, but urgency does not remove their defensive problems. Wrexham's better balance earns a cautious preference.", "fc-20261121-33": "Swansea sit sixth but have lost four of five and conceded 11. West Brom are unbeaten in five, scoring 11 and most recently beating Millwall without conceding. The table gap is small; the form gap favours West Brom.", "fc-20261121-34": "Middlesbrough are second with 29 points and scored ten in five, despite going winless in their last two. Bristol City arrive after a five-goal loss to Norwich and two straight defeats. The hosts' stronger attacking base and home advantage favour Middlesbrough.", "fc-20261121-35": "West Ham are winless in four and cannot treat the bottom club lightly. Preston beat Southampton without conceding, but that followed four winless games and they still have only eight points. Both carry risk; West Ham receive a cautious home preference.", "fc-20261121-36": "Wolves are unbeaten in five and conceded only three, holding fourth place on 28 points. Charlton's win over Sheffield United ended four defeats but does not erase ten conceded in five. Wolves' sustained defensive and results record makes them the selection.", "fc-20261121-37": "Sheffield United's loss to Charlton ended four unbeaten games. Watford held Middlesbrough goalless and conceded only four in five, so the hosts may need patience. Sheffield United's three wins in five and home advantage earn a narrow preference.", "fc-20261116-01": "For Germany, the night in Berlin carries greater weight than a normal home fixture. Third in the group with eight points, they need a positive result against leaders Netherlands and hope to build on a three-goal away win over Serbia. Germany's last five produced two wins, two draws and one defeat, but their inability to score against Greece in two meetings shows that a well-organised defence can still frustrate them. Netherlands lead on eleven points, remain unbeaten in five and recently scored seven against Greece. Germany cannot press with so many players that they leave spaces for the visitors to exploit. Their ability to keep a compact shape while taking control could determine the match. Despite Dutch momentum, Germany's improved finishing in Serbia and the urgency of a home response make **Germany my selection.**", "fc-20261116-02": "The central question for Greece is how quickly they can recover from a seven-goal defeat in the Netherlands. Before that collapse they had gone four group games unbeaten, including victory away to Germany, so one disastrous result should not erase their underlying form. Greece still sit second with eight points and have their fate largely in their own hands. Serbia have lost all five group matches and conceded three against Germany most recently. Their first task is therefore to restore defensive stability rather than launch sustained pressure on the hosts. Greece must avoid a reckless attacking response that would expose a shaken back line. If they manage the game patiently and choose their openings, they can punish Serbia's repeated defensive errors. Allowing for the psychological cost of their latest loss, stronger group form and home advantage still make **Greece my selection.**", "fc-20261116-03": "North Macedonia remain without a point ahead of their final group match, reflecting persistent problems in both finishing and defending. They scored once away to Scotland but could not prevent defeat, and failed to score in either of their two home fixtures. There is little recent evidence of a quick turnaround. Slovenia sit second on eight points and their latest goalless draw with Switzerland demonstrated an ability to contain even the group leaders. They have also won away to Scotland, so playing on the road is no reason to underestimate them. The hosts may play with added urgency in pursuit of their first point, which means Slovenia should stay patient early on. Even allowing for that final-match motivation, the contrast between five straight Macedonian defeats and Slovenia's steadier results makes **Slovenia my selection.**", "fc-20261116-04": "Switzerland have been the group's most reliable side, taking thirteen points from four wins and one draw in five fixtures. They failed to score on their latest visit to Slovenia, but were productive in their previous four matches and have won both home games. Scotland sit third with seven points and travel with confidence after beating North Macedonia, yet defeats to Slovenia and Switzerland illustrate their difficulty against the group's stronger teams. An early Swiss goal could force the visitors to attack more openly and allow the hosts to control proceedings. Scotland must defend carefully at the start and make the most of limited chances. Switzerland's unbeaten record, home results and more effective finishing throughout the campaign make **Switzerland my selection.**", "fc-20261116-05": "The Faroe Islands need to turn resilience into victory. They have drawn all five group games, remaining unbeaten but collecting only five points and sitting third. A home win over seven-point Moldova is necessary to climb above the visitors. Their latest two-goal draw away to Slovakia showed they can respond under pressure, although they must now turn chances into decisive goals. Moldova are better placed in the table and will look to make the game uncomfortable for the hosts. A sixth draw would do little to solve the Faroes' problem, but rushing forward could open dangerous spaces. If the home side remain patient, protect possession and use their recent fighting spirit, they have a route to three points. Given the home incentive and competitive record, **Faroe Islands are my selection.**", "fc-20261116-06": "Kazakhstan are bottom of their group with two points after five matches and are still searching for a first victory. Defeat away to Moldova again showed their difficulty in turning encouraging draws against the Faroe Islands into sustained progress. Slovakia lead with eleven points, having won three and drawn two without defeat. Their four goals away to Moldova underline a more reliable attacking threat, even if their own defence has occasionally been tested. Kazakhstan will need an organised start and greater precision when opportunities arise; the visitors should avoid taking control for granted. Comparing the sides' ability to create chances, accumulate points and manage difficult away games, **Slovakia are my selection.**", "fc-20261116-07": "Estonia have built their campaign around defensive discipline rather than heavy scoring. Two wins and three draws in five matches have earned them nine points, and four consecutive clean sheets give them a strong platform for this home game. Bulgaria have four points and enter after conceding five in their most recent defeat. They will need to find a way through a home defence that has been hard to break down. Estonia are not especially prolific, so patience and careful game management will matter more than taking unnecessary risks in pursuit of an early goal. The hosts' unbeaten record, second-place standing and defensive consistency make **Estonia my selection.**", "fc-20261116-08": "Iceland lead the group with eleven points heading into the final fixture and arrive at their most confident attacking moment after scoring five away to Bulgaria. Four consecutive clean sheets show that the lead has not been built on goals alone. Luxembourg won their opener but have since lost four straight games and failed to score in the last three. The visitors, fourth with three points, must avoid conceding early, yet sitting deep for the entire match could simply invite prolonged Icelandic pressure. The hosts still need disciplined preparation rather than assuming the result is secured. Recent finishing, defensive resilience and the clear gap between the teams' group performances all point towards **Iceland as my selection.**", "fc-20261116-09": "Lithuania have four points from three group matches and sit second, with a final home fixture offering an opportunity to finish with a victory. A goalless friendly against Suriname showed that they still need to sharpen their attack, but a recent three-goal win over Andorra demonstrates what they can produce on home soil. Liechtenstein have only one group point and failed to score in their last five games, leaving problems at both ends of the pitch. Their goalless away draw with Azerbaijan is a warning that an impatient host can still be frustrated. Lithuania must construct chances carefully and use any lead to control the match. Home advantage and the difference in attacking output make **Lithuania my selection.**", "fc-20261116-10": "Gibraltar enter the final group game still seeking their first victory, but must face an unbeaten Malta side. The hosts are third with two points and failed to score in their latest defeat away to Andorra, making a stronger attacking display essential. Malta lead the group with seven points after three wins and two draws in their last five. Victories over Andorra both home and away underline their ability to manage tight games. Gibraltar did earn a draw in Malta, so the visitors cannot afford complacency simply because they lead the table. An organised opening by the hosts could keep the contest close. Nevertheless, Malta's recent winning habits and unbeaten run make **Malta my selection.**", "fc-20261116-11": "Albacete's recent form no longer reflects their lowly league position. They remain twenty-first with ten points, yet consecutive league victories over Eldense, Sabadell and Leganes, followed by a three-goal cup performance, show clear momentum. Celta Fortuna are seventeenth on thirteen points but have gone four matches without winning and lost their last two away fixtures, at Girona and Burgos. Conceding five at Girona raises concerns over how they will handle a home attack growing in confidence. Albacete's poor season record should not be ignored, yet their recent conversion of chances has improved markedly. Giving more weight to current direction and home advantage than the table alone, **Albacete are my selection.**", "fc-20261122-01": "Hull have drawn three of their last five and lost narrowly at Arsenal, so breaking them down will require patience. However, they are winless across that sequence and sit 14th with 11 points. Brighton are second on 22 points and have beaten Brentford, Getafe and Manchester City without conceding in their last three matches. The visitors' defensive consistency and stronger recent winning record make Brighton the selection.", "fc-20261122-02": "Liverpool regained confidence by winning at Crystal Palace after defeats to Arsenal and Fenerbahce. Fifth with 18 points, they also have Frimpong and Gravenberch back in training. United begin life under Mauricio Pochettino in 19th on eight points, with one win and 15 goals conceded in their last five competitive games. A new-manager response is possible, but those defensive problems cannot be assumed to disappear immediately. Liverpool at Anfield are the selection.", "fc-20261122-03": "Juventus are unbeaten in three after wins over Napoli and AZ and a draw at Fiorentina. Seventh with 18 points, they need to turn that recovery into a sustained league run. Venezia beat Udinese last time, but have lost nine of eleven league games and their last two away matches without scoring. Spalletti's side should be able to build pressure at home, especially if they score first. Juventus are the selection.", "fc-20261122-04": "Bologna have won their last four league games and are ninth on 17 points. After losing to Inter, their four-goal away win at Milan demonstrated a strong recovery, but Udinese arrive with a much less convincing threat. Bottom with five points, the visitors have lost four and drawn one of their last five, failing to score in four. Bologna's recovery and home advantage make them the selection.", "fc-20261122-05": "Sassuolo have conceded 19 goals in five matches and lost their last four, leaving them 16th with eight points. An open game could expose the same spaces exploited by Lazio and Fiorentina. Genoa also lost last time, but wins over Lecce and Venezia give them a firmer recent base and 13 points. Neither defence inspires complete confidence; Genoa are the selection because Sassuolo's repeated concessions create the clearer weakness.", "fc-20261122-06": "Only four points separate fifth-placed Milan and sixth-placed Frosinone. Milan have won three of five but recent home defeats to Bologna and Ferencvaros show that control can slip. Frosinone have scored freely against Lecce, Torino, Sassuolo and Atalanta, although they lost at Cagliari last time. This should be competitive, but Amorim's Milan have the greater opportunity to decide it at San Siro. Milan are the selection.", "fc-20261122-07": "Atalanta have scored eight and conceded ten in five matches, illustrating the gap between their attacking threat and defensive security. They are 11th with 14 points, while Inter are third with 28. Inter lost the Milan derby but have won four of five and kept three clean sheets. Atalanta can threaten at home, yet the visitors offer the stronger balance at both ends. Inter are the selection.", "fc-20261122-08": "Barcelona lead with 33 points from 12 matches and have won eleven league games, including their latest visit to Atletico. Villarreal beat Getafe without conceding last time but lost at home to Espanyol in their previous league match but were heavily exposed by PSG in Europe. Christensen is unavailable and Cubarsi needs careful management, while Kounde, De Jong and Olmo are available again. Villarreal demand patience, but Barcelona's home attacking pressure makes them the selection.", "fc-20261122-09": "Racing recovered with a win at Malaga but are 12th on 14 points after defensive problems elsewhere. Sociedad are fifth with 22 and have won three of five, including a narrow victory over Rayo last time. Their defeat at Athletic warns against assuming every away visit will be straightforward. Racing can respond at home, but Sociedad's stronger attacking base makes them the selection.", "fc-20261122-10": "Osasuna need this home opportunity to improve on 16th place and 12 points. Their cup win over lower-level opposition should not be mistaken for proof of dominant league attacking form. Malaga, however, remain winless after 12 league games with five points and lost at home to Racing last time. Osasuna's recent draw with Athletic offers a better foundation. The home side are the selection.", "fc-20261122-11": "Getafe have a home win over Sevilla to encourage them, but scoreless defeats at Athletic and Villarreal expose an inconsistent attack. Atletico lost to Barcelona last time, having also lost to Bayern, although earlier clean-sheet league wins over Levante and Deportivo support their wider league position. Third with 28 points, they have the stronger platform for controlling a tight contest. Getafe's home resistance is a concern, but Atletico are the selection.", "fc-20261122-12": "Augsburg conceded five at Leipzig and are 15th with nine points. Their only win in five came in the cup, while Mainz also arrive after consecutive league defeats and have just one point more. This is a close, vulnerable matchup rather than a confident away proposition. Augsburg's recent defensive exposure creates a narrow case for Mainz, who are the selection.", "fc-20261122-13": "Werder enter the northern derby sixth with 15 points. Before their defeat at Stuttgart they beat Hoffenheim without conceding and scored three at Mainz. Hamburg won last time against Gladbach but consecutive league and cup defeats to Frankfurt exposed defensive problems. Derby intensity reduces the value of simple table comparisons, yet Werder's home advantage and continuity after Thioune's renewal give them the edge. Werder are the selection.", "fc-20261122-14": "Paris FC are third with 20 points and have won three of five, including their latest trip to Auxerre. Home wins over Monaco and Rennes support their case here. Angers are 17th with eight points and have lost four and drawn one of five, with little attacking output. Paris can concede, so a clean sheet is not assumed, but their stronger recent results make them the selection.", "fc-20261122-15": "Only one point separates Lorient and Rennes. Lorient won at Le Havre but have lost two of their last three home games. Rennes' defeats to Lille and Nice argue for caution, although their win over Strasbourg and draw at Juventus show a useful attacking threat. This is a narrow judgment rather than a clear mismatch. Rennes are the selection for their ability to create a decisive chance.", "fc-20261122-16": "Marseille have won four of five, including successive away victories at Leverkusen and Lens, and are fifth with 18 points. Le Mans have held Monaco and Auxerre but lost without scoring at Troyes and sit 16th with eight points. The visitors can frustrate, so Marseille should avoid forcing the game too early. Their stronger momentum and home pressure make Marseille the selection.", "fc-20261122-17": "Burnley are winless in five and conceded five at Cardiff, leaving them 22nd with ten points. Blackburn have 21 points in 13th and have beaten West Ham and Wrexham but lost to Stoke in their last five. Their away losses at Swansea and West Brom are a warning, and a derby increases uncertainty, but Blackburn's recent ability to win is substantially stronger. Blackburn are the selection.", "fc-20261122-18": "Cottbus have drawn three of five but won none, leaving them 14th with 11 points. Hertha lead with 31 points from ten wins and one draw in eleven league matches. Four wins in their last five, including a convincing away success at Kaiserslautern, underline that strength. Cottbus may resist early, but Hertha are better equipped to maintain pressure. Hertha are the selection.", "fc-20261122-19": "Kaiserslautern recovered from defeat to Hertha by winning at Osnabruck. Fifth with 21 points, they have four wins and four clean sheets in five matches. Dresden won convincingly last time but away losses at Hannover and Kiel reveal a less stable base. The visitors should be more confident, yet Kaiserslautern's recent defensive discipline makes the home side the selection.", "fc-20261122-20": "Both teams have 11 points near the bottom. Karlsruhe have suffered heavy away defeats but won their last two home matches against Heidenheim and Darmstadt. Osnabruck have only one win in five and lost at home to Kaiserslautern last time. Neither side offers broad consistency; the difference is Karlsruhe's more encouraging recent home record. Karlsruhe are the selection.", "fc-20261124-01": "Bodø/Glimt sit 25th with four points from four Champions League matches and have conceded more than they have scored. LASK are 16th on six points after consecutive wins in the competition. Although Bodø/Glimt have home advantage, LASK's recent form suggests that a heavy defeat is unlikely. **LASK are my selection.**", "fc-20261124-02": "Galatasaray sit 18th with six points after consecutive Champions League victories. Unai Emery's Aston Villa are sixth on nine points and have been strong in attack. However, Villa may find it difficult to attack freely at Galatasaray's ground, and both sides may prioritise securing points. **Under is my selection.**", "fc-20261124-03": "Arteta's Arsenal remain unbeaten in the Champions League, sitting third with ten points. Their defensive stability is a key strength, but Dortmund have also won three of four games. Arsenal may have the advantage at home, yet beating Dortmund by a large margin will not be easy. **Dortmund are my selection.**", "fc-20261124-04": "Como have impressed in attack in this season's Champions League. Douvikas's finishing and Nico Paz's creativity could cause difficulties for AEK Athens' defence. AEK have defensive weaknesses but can score in reply. **Over is my selection.**", "fc-20261124-05": "Feyenoord and Porto have only three Champions League points each, so both need a win. Feyenoord have been conceding frequently, while Porto have gained confidence in attack. Both sides could open up in search of victory and have defensive weaknesses. **Over is my selection.**", "fc-20261124-06": "Manchester City have scored 12 goals in four Champions League games and sit seventh with nine points. Napoli have conceded frequently and could struggle to contain an attack led by Haaland. Napoli also have attacking quality through De Bruyne, McTominay and Højlund, so both teams could score. **Over is my selection.**", "fc-20261124-07": "Leipzig and Lens have struggled for Champions League results, but Lens's defensive weaknesses are more pronounced. Leipzig can score and should be able to put Lens under pressure at home. Given Lens's defensive and away difficulties, **Leipzig are my selection.**", "fc-20261124-08": "Real Madrid have won all four Champions League games and possess a strong attack. PSV, however, can defend in an organised manner and make life difficult for Madrid. Madrid may win, but a wide winning margin will not be easy. **PSV are my selection.**", "fc-20261124-09": "Slovan Bratislava have lost all four Champions League matches and struggled in both attack and defence. Real Betis have nine points, and Isco and Antony's creativity could threaten Slovan's back line. The difference in form suggests a sizeable winning margin is possible. **Real Betis are my selection.**", "fc-20261124-10": "Bristol City are 18th on 18 points and have won only one of their last five games, struggling for results at home. Wrexham are 14th on 21 points and unbeaten in three. Comparing their recent form and consistency, **Wrexham are my selection.**", "fc-20261124-11": "Cardiff are unbeaten in eight home matches this season and have secured good home results. Preston sit bottom on nine points and have conceded frequently. Weighing Cardiff's home form against Preston's weaknesses, **Cardiff are my selection.**", "fc-20261124-12": "Charlton and Lincoln sit near the bottom of the table and have each lost four of their last five. Both struggle to finish chances and may play cautiously to avoid losing points near the relegation zone. With both attacks struggling, **Under is my selection.**", "fc-20261124-13": "Middlesbrough lead the table with 32 points and 32 goals in 16 games, and remain unbeaten at home. Swansea's recent results have dipped, but they retain the ability to score. Given Middlesbrough's home scoring and Swansea's ability to respond, **Over is my selection.**", "fc-20261124-14": "Norwich have won five consecutive league matches and are in strong attacking form. QPR sit seventh and have lost only one of their last five. With both sides in good form and possessing attacking quality, both could score. **Over is my selection.**", "fc-20261124-15": "Portsmouth have lost only one of their last five and have been consistent. West Ham possess attacking quality but have gone five games without a win. Although West Ham have the stronger squad, Portsmouth's recent form and home advantage make them appealing. **Portsmouth are my selection.**", "fc-20261124-16": "Sheffield United sit ninth on 25 points, while Southampton are sixth on 27. Southampton's defensive stability may make it difficult for Sheffield United to score, but the hosts will not give in easily at home. In a closely matched contest, **Under is my selection.**", "fc-20261124-17": "Wolves sit third on 31 points and have won four and drawn one of their last five. Derby are 23rd on ten points, weak in attack and conceding frequently. Wolves' current form and home attack suggest that a wide winning margin is possible. **Wolves are my selection.**", "fc-20261125-01": "Sabah have three points from four European matches and must protect their defensive shape after a heavy defeat at Viking. Barcelona arrive with four consecutive wins, including their latest success against Villarreal. Hansi Flick's side should control possession; Sabah's counterattacks remain a threat, but Barcelona's attacking quality makes them the selection. Lamine Yamal is absent with an ankle problem, according to the official travelling squad update.", "fc-20261125-02": "Slavia have won their last two domestic matches but have one point and Villarreal three after four Champions League games. Villarreal's heavy loss to PSG exposed their defence, but scoring twice against Barcelona showed their attacking threat. Slavia's home pressure could leave openings, so Villarreal are the selection in a difficult contest.", "fc-20261125-03": "Atlético and Viking both have four European points. Viking's draw with Bayern and win over Sabah underline their attacking threat, although their latest domestic defeat is a concern. Atlético recovered with a clean-sheet win over Getafe and should control more of this home match. Atlético are the selection.", "fc-20261125-04": "Both clubs have nine European points. Brugge are unbeaten in five and arrive after a large win at Mechelen, while Liverpool's convincing victory over Manchester United has restored attacking confidence. The visitors must avoid the defensive lapses seen at Fenerbahce, but their threat in open spaces makes Liverpool the selection.", "fc-20261125-05": "Inter have six European points, one fewer than Stuttgart. Their four-goal draw with Atalanta showed both attacking strength and defensive vulnerability. Stuttgart have kept clean sheets in their last two matches but lost their previous European away game at Galatasaray. Inter's home advantage and attacking options make them the selection.", "fc-20261125-06": "Lille have only one European point and failed to score in their latest defeat to Lyon. Bayern remain unbeaten in the competition and in their last five matches, including a European away win at Atlético. Lille may keep the game tight, but Bayern have more ways to create the decisive chance and are the selection. Harry Kane is unavailable with an ankle ligament injury; Bayern must adapt their attack.", "fc-20261125-07": "PSG have won all four European matches and their last five fixtures. Roma bring strong attacking form of their own after a convincing win over Parma, but have only four European points and conceded three at Manchester United. PSG must stay alert to transitions; their home pressure and chance creation still make them the selection.", "fc-20261125-08": "Shakhtar have failed to score in their last two European defeats. Fenerbahce's win over Liverpool showed greater attacking potential, although their latest domestic draw exposed defensive weaknesses. The visitors must be patient against a compact opponent, but Fenerbahce are the selection for their stronger recent European attacking display.", "fc-20261125-09": "Sporting have four consecutive clean-sheet wins and nine European points. Manchester United arrive after a heavy defeat at Liverpool, leaving Mauricio Pochettino with immediate defensive work. Their comeback against Roma shows attacking potential, but Sporting's organisation and home advantage make the Portuguese side the selection.", "fc-20261125-10": "Bolton are nineteenth with 18 points and have won only once in five. Fifth-placed West Brom have 29 points and are unbeaten in five, with wins over Millwall and West Ham. Their tendency to draw means patience is needed, but Bolton's defensive problems make West Brom the selection.", "fc-20261125-11": "Burnley have one win from sixteen league games and none in their last five. Birmingham remain fourth with 29 points despite losing at Stoke, following three consecutive wins. Burnley's draws make this awkward, but Birmingham's stronger season and recent performances make them the selection.", "fc-20261125-12": "Watford's heavy defeat at Sheffield United and limited recent scoring undermine their home advantage. Blackburn also concede too often, but are unbeaten in two after beating West Ham. The game could remain close for long spells; Blackburn's more convincing recent goal threat makes them the selection.", "fc-20261125-13": "Stoke are third with 32 points and four consecutive wins, most recently a clean-sheet victory over Birmingham. Millwall have lost three in a row without scoring. They may defend deep and rely on set pieces, but Stoke's confidence and ability to sustain pressure make the home side the selection.", "fc-20261125-14": "Cremonese need to respond after losing at Südtirol, which ended a three-match winning run. Fifth-placed Avellino are unbeaten in four and arrive after a convincing victory over Mantova. Cremonese can press at home, but Avellino's current resilience and attacking confidence make the visitors the selection.", "fc-20261125-15": "Mantova are seventh but winless in four after a heavy defeat to Avellino. Arezzo have also struggled, with no wins and three defeats in their last five. Neither attack offers strong certainty; Mantova must rebuild their defensive confidence, but home advantage gives them the edge and makes them the selection.", "fc-20261125-16": "Padova are unbeaten in five but have drawn their last three. Sampdoria have won three in succession, conceding only once in those victories. The hosts should make this competitive, yet Sampdoria's sharper recent finishing and improved defensive results make them the selection.", "fc-20261125-17": "Pisa ended a four-game winless run by beating Empoli. Modena, second with 26 points, have four wins and a draw in five and clean sheets in their last two. Pisa's home advantage matters, but Modena's more consistent defending and attacking returns make them the selection.", "fc-20261126-02": "Celta Vigo are 27 with 3 points; AFC Bournemouth are 2 with 12 points. Recent official five-game records: home 1W/1D/3L, scoring 7 and conceding 7; away 5W/0D/0L, scoring 12 and conceding 2. Celta are without injured Borja Iglesias, Carl Starfelt and Miguel Roman, reducing options in both attack and defence. Bournemouth’s five consecutive wins and limited concessions provide a more stable foundation. They can look to exploit space when Celta push forward. AFC Bournemouth is my selection.", "fc-20261126-04": "Olympiacos are 6 with 10 points; AC Milan are 28 with 3 points. Recent official five-game records: home 3W/2D/0L, scoring 15 and conceding 5; away 3W/0D/2L, scoring 12 and conceding 9. Olympiacos can apply pressure at home, while Milan have attacking confidence after scoring five against Frosinone. Amorim nevertheless acknowledges that Milan’s defending needs improvement. The attacking output and need for points suggest chances at both ends. Over is my selection.", "fc-20261126-09": "Crystal Palace are 21 with 5 points; Real Sociedad are 20 with 5 points. Recent official five-game records: home 1W/1D/3L, scoring 5 and conceding 9; away 2W/1D/2L, scoring 7 and conceding 7. Palace are developing Thomas Frank’s approach, while Sociedad’s recent results are also mixed. Equal European points give both sides reason to avoid costly errors. A contested midfield and fewer clear chances support a restrained game. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261126-01": "Besiktas are 8 with 7 points; Hapoel Be'er are 33 with 1 points. Available European-only records are used for Hapoel Be'er. Recent official five-game records: home 3W/1D/1L, scoring 13 and conceding 7; away 0W/1D/4L, scoring 3 and conceding 13. Besiktas have shown sustained scoring ability and can seek to dictate the tempo at home. Hapoel’s available European records show frequent concessions, making prolonged home pressure a concern. Converting early chances would allow the hosts to maintain control. Besiktas is my selection.", "fc-20261126-03": "Dinamo Zagreb are 9 with 7 points; Bayer Leverkusen are 7 with 9 points. Available European-only records are used for Dinamo Zagreb. Recent official five-game records: home 2W/1D/2L, scoring 6 and conceding 7; away 3W/0D/2L, scoring 13 and conceding 8. Dinamo can try to raise the tempo at home but must contain Leverkusen’s recent scoring output. The visitors arrive after consecutive wins and have regained attacking rhythm. Their combination play and ability to convert chances support the selection. Bayer Leverkusen is my selection.", "fc-20261126-05": "Marseille are 31 with 3 points; Levski Sofia are 10 with 7 points. Available European-only records are used for Levski Sofia. Recent official five-game records: home 4W/0D/1L, scoring 11 and conceding 7; away 2W/1D/2L, scoring 4 and conceding 7. Marseille’s latest defeat followed four straight wins, so one result does not erase that earlier progress. Levski have collected European points and should not be dismissed. The hosts’ pressure and recent scoring ability remain persuasive. Marseille is my selection.", "fc-20261126-06": "RB Salzburg are 26 with 4 points; Ararat-Armenia are 36 with 0 points. Available European-only records are used for Ararat-Armenia. Recent official five-game records: home 3W/0D/2L, scoring 12 and conceding 8; away 1W/0D/4L, scoring 5 and conceding 14. Salzburg retain an attacking foundation despite losing their latest match. Ararat-Armenia’s concessions in the available official records offer an opening. Maintaining discipline after turnovers would help the hosts sustain control. RB Salzburg is my selection.", "fc-20261126-07": "Union St.-Gilloise are 4 with 10 points; Lech Poznan are 35 with 1 points. Available European-only records are used for Lech Poznan. Recent official five-game records: home 5W/0D/0L, scoring 11 and conceding 4; away 0W/2D/3L, scoring 4 and conceding 14. Union have won five straight games and limited concessions in their latest fixtures. Lech have struggled for victories in the available official records. The combination of attacking momentum and defensive stability favours the hosts. Union St.-Gilloise is my selection.", "fc-20261126-08": "Viktoria Plzen are 30 with 3 points; Benfica are 1 with 12 points. Available European-only records are used for Viktoria Plzen. Recent official five-game records: home 2W/0D/3L, scoring 8 and conceding 8; away 5W/0D/0L, scoring 12 and conceding 5. Benfica have won five straight matches, but Plzen can seek to reduce space at home. The visitors may control possession patiently when ahead. A cautious home approach and controlled visiting play support a more restrained scoring contest. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261126-10": "Ferencvaros are 3 with 12 points; NK Celje are 25 with 4 points. Available European-only records are used for Ferencvaros and NK Celje. Recent official five-game records: home 5W/0D/0L, scoring 15 and conceding 3; away 1W/1D/3L, scoring 6 and conceding 11. Ferencvaros have sustained a winning run both recently and in the Europa League. Celje’s recent defeats may affect confidence. Early home pressure and the ability to maintain attacking rhythm support Ferencvaros. Ferencvaros is my selection.", "fc-20261126-11": "Juventus are 5 with 10 points; Omonia Nicosia are 18 with 6 points. Available European-only records are used for Omonia Nicosia. Recent official five-game records: home 3W/1D/1L, scoring 10 and conceding 5; away 3W/0D/2L, scoring 10 and conceding 9. Juventus can expect more possession, while Omonia may prioritise closing space after consecutive defeats. Defensive discipline should be important to the visitors. Home control, rather than an uncontrolled exchange, supports a lower-scoring assessment. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261126-12": "NEC Nijmegen are 12 with 7 points; Stade Rennais are 17 with 6 points. Recent official five-game records: home 2W/1D/2L, scoring 9 and conceding 10; away 1W/2D/2L, scoring 7 and conceding 8. NEC and Rennes have inconsistent recent records, encouraging an emphasis on avoiding errors. Rennes need to reorganise quickly after losing possession away from home. Midfield contests and defensive obstruction may outweigh clean finishing opportunities. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261126-13": "OFI Crete are 16 with 6 points; Anderlecht are 15 with 6 points. Recent official five-game records: home 3W/1D/1L, scoring 5 and conceding 3; away 3W/1D/1L, scoring 8 and conceding 6. Crete and Anderlecht have equal European points, making this difficult to separate. The hosts can try to close space and disrupt the visitors’ combinations. Protecting points could lead to fewer openings. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261126-14": "Lyon are 13 with 7 points; Lillestrom are 34 with 1 points. Recent official five-game records: home 2W/1D/2L, scoring 4 and conceding 5; away 4W/0D/1L, scoring 9 and conceding 5. Lyon have the stronger European position, but Lillestrom’s recent victories deserve respect. The visitors can defend patiently and choose their moments. Home possession control and visiting caution support a restrained contest. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261126-15": "Torreense are 19 with 6 points; Celtic are 32 with 3 points. Recent official five-game records: home 2W/0D/3L, scoring 8 and conceding 12; away 3W/1D/1L, scoring 10 and conceding 7. Celtic arrive after three consecutive wins and with greater confidence. Torreense still struggle to reproduce positive results consistently. The visitors’ ability to convert their opportunities supports Celtic. Celtic is my selection.", "fc-20261126-16": "Sparta Prague are 22 with 4 points; AZ Alkmaar are 14 with 6 points. Available European-only records are used for Sparta Prague. Recent official five-game records: home 1W/1D/3L, scoring 6 and conceding 9; away 2W/0D/3L, scoring 10 and conceding 9. Sparta and AZ have not provided a consistently dependable defensive picture. Both need European points and may have to take the initiative. More transitions from midfield into attack could create scoring opportunities. Over is my selection.", "fc-20261126-17": "Sunderland are 11 with 7 points; Jagiellonia Bialystok are 29 with 3 points. Available European-only records are used for Jagiellonia Bialystok. Recent official five-game records: home 2W/1D/2L, scoring 5 and conceding 7; away 2W/0D/3L, scoring 6 and conceding 8. Sunderland’s recent results do not establish a consistently reliable attack. Jagiellonia can try to reduce the tempo and deny space. The available European records and finishing patterns favour caution over a free-scoring exchange. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261126-18": "TSG Hoffenheim are 23 with 4 points; SK Sturm Graz are 24 with 4 points. Recent official five-game records: home 1W/2D/2L, scoring 4 and conceding 6; away 0W/2D/3L, scoring 8 and conceding 11. Hoffenheim and Sturm have equal European points and need a win. Their recent records do not establish a dependable attacking advantage. A cautious start could leave midfield contests more prominent than clear chances. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261126-19": "Kairat Almaty are 27 with 2 points; Mjällby AIF are 9 with 7 points. Available European-only records are used for Kairat Almaty. Recent official five-game records: home 0W/2D/3L, scoring 3 and conceding 13; away 2W/3D/0L, scoring 5 and conceding 2. Kairat are winless in five while Mjallby are unbeaten over the same span. Home support can lift the tempo, but wasted chances may increase pressure on Kairat. The visitors’ resilience supports the selection. Mjällby AIF is my selection.", "fc-20261126-20": "Ajax Amsterdam are 11 with 6 points; FC Thun are 20 with 3 points. Available European-only records are used for FC Thun. Recent official five-game records: home 4W/1D/0L, scoring 14 and conceding 4; away 1W/1D/3L, scoring 5 and conceding 12. Ajax have won frequently and can seek possession control at home. Thun may defend compactly rather than open the game immediately. If the hosts manage a lead patiently, an end-to-end attacking contest need not develop. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261126-21": "SK Brann are 6 with 7 points; AGF are 24 with 2 points. Recent official five-game records: home 2W/2D/1L, scoring 12 and conceding 11; away 3W/1D/1L, scoring 6 and conceding 4. Brann and AGF show limited recent separation, with draws in their records. Both need to restrict space after losing the ball. A game built around waiting for mistakes could be more cautious than open. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261126-22": "Brighton & Hove Albion are 5 with 7 points; CSU Craiova are 8 with 7 points. Available European-only records are used for CSU Craiova. Recent official five-game records: home 3W/1D/1L, scoring 6 and conceding 4; away 2W/2D/1L, scoring 7 and conceding 4. Brighton and Craiova have equal European points, so the visitors deserve respect. Regrouping behind the ball could force the hosts to build attacks patiently. Possession control need not turn this into a wide-open game. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261126-23": "Egnatia are 26 with 2 points; Lincoln Red Imps are 22 with 3 points. Available European-only records are used for Egnatia and Lincoln Red Imps. Recent official five-game records: home 0W/3D/2L, scoring 3 and conceding 6; away 2W/0D/3L, scoring 6 and conceding 8. Egnatia’s five-game winless sequence raises questions about attacking confidence. Lincoln can prioritise closing space away from home. Recent scoring output and cautious game management support fewer clear openings. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261126-24": "Jablonec are 23 with 2 points; FC Lugano are 1 with 9 points. Available European-only records are used for Jablonec and FC Lugano. Recent official five-game records: home 1W/2D/2L, scoring 4 and conceding 5; away 4W/1D/0L, scoring 14 and conceding 6. Lugano have won all three European games, while Jablonec have struggled for points. That record provides confidence in the visitors’ approach. Patience under home pressure and better use of chances support Lugano. FC Lugano is my selection.", "fc-20261126-25": "Heart of Midlothian are 32 with 1 points; AS Monaco are 4 with 9 points. Recent official five-game records: home 1W/1D/3L, scoring 14 and conceding 12; away 1W/3D/1L, scoring 6 and conceding 6. Hearts need points at home, and Monaco’s recent record does not establish complete defensive reliability. Both may commit players when attacking opportunities arise. Changes in momentum and chances at either end support goals. Over is my selection.", "fc-20261126-26": "Iberia 1999 are 29 with 1 points; Getafe are 31 with 1 points. Available European-only records are used for Iberia 1999. Recent official five-game records: home 0W/1D/4L, scoring 3 and conceding 11; away 2W/0D/3L, scoring 6 and conceding 9. Iberia have struggled for wins, while Getafe’s recent results also raise questions about attacking consistency. Both need organisation and defensive recovery to avoid an early setback. Contested possession may outweigh precise finishing. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261126-27": "Kauno Zalgiris are 36 with 0 points; Riga FC are 19 with 3 points. Available European-only records are used for Kauno Zalgiris and Riga FC. Recent official five-game records: home 1W/0D/4L, scoring 2 and conceding 14; away 1W/4D/0L, scoring 5 and conceding 4. Zalgiris have lost their latest three games, while Riga are unbeaten in the five available official records. Frequent home concessions offer opportunities to the visitors. Riga’s ability to remain competitive under pressure supports the selection. Riga FC is my selection.", "fc-20261126-28": "Pafos are 30 with 1 points; FC Midtjylland are 34 with 1 points. Available European-only records are used for Pafos. Recent official five-game records: home 1W/2D/2L, scoring 8 and conceding 10; away 3W/1D/1L, scoring 11 and conceding 12. Pafos and Midtjylland both need European points, making prolonged passivity difficult. Their recent records include goals scored and conceded. Opening up in search of a win could create chances at both ends. Over is my selection.", "fc-20261126-29": "CSKA Sofia are 28 with 1 points; Trabzonspor are 12 with 6 points. Available European-only records are used for CSKA Sofia. Recent official five-game records: home 0W/1D/4L, scoring 4 and conceding 11; away 4W/0D/1L, scoring 9 and conceding 4. CSKA Sofia have struggled for wins, while Trabzonspor have more victories in their official records. The hosts may prioritise rebuilding defensive organisation, and the visitors can manage the game when ahead. Discipline and tempo control support a restrained contest. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261126-30": "Borac Banja Luka are 21 with 3 points; Atalanta are 16 with 4 points. Available European-only records are used for Borac Banja Luka. Recent official five-game records: home 3W/0D/2L, scoring 9 and conceding 6; away 1W/3D/1L, scoring 8 and conceding 10. Atalanta have one win in five, compared with three for Borac in the available official records. Disciplined home regrouping could force the visitors to build chances patiently. Atalanta can threaten, but home resilience and selective attacking opportunities support Borac. Borac Banja Luka is my selection.", "fc-20261126-31": "Hajduk Split are 13 with 6 points; Sint-Truidense are 10 with 7 points. Available European-only records are used for Hajduk Split. Recent official five-game records: home 3W/1D/1L, scoring 8 and conceding 6; away 1W/2D/2L, scoring 10 and conceding 9. Hajduk have three wins in the available official five-game record. Sint-Truidense have fewer recent victories and need to improve their control of concessions. Home pressure and the use of chances provide a modest preference for Hajduk. Hajduk Split is my selection.", "fc-20261126-32": "Inter D'Escaldes are 35 with 0 points; F.C. København are 7 with 7 points. Available European-only records are used for Inter D'Escaldes. Recent official five-game records: home 0W/2D/3L, scoring 4 and conceding 9; away 3W/1D/1L, scoring 6 and conceding 7. Copenhagen can seek control, but Inter d’Escaldes may keep their defence compact. The hosts need to reduce the tempo rather than open the game hastily. Visiting possession and home defensive emphasis support a controlled contest. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261126-33": "KAA Gent are 18 with 4 points; Red Star Belgrade are 15 with 4 points. Available European-only records are used for Red Star Belgrade. Recent official five-game records: home 2W/1D/2L, scoring 5 and conceding 3; away 2W/1D/2L, scoring 10 and conceding 11. Gent and Red Star have equal European points, but home support can help Gent apply early pressure. The visitors need disciplined recovery after losing possession. The difference is limited, with a modest preference for home control. KAA Gent is my selection.", "fc-20261126-34": "FC Nordsjælland are 25 with 2 points; Panathinaikos are 2 with 9 points. Recent official five-game records: home 2W/1D/2L, scoring 14 and conceding 7; away 5W/0D/0L, scoring 9 and conceding 2. Panathinaikos have five straight wins and a strong defensive record, but Nordsjaelland have scored heavily in their latest two games. Home attacking momentum can test the visitors, who also have the form to respond. Their different strengths could create opportunities at both ends. Over is my selection.", "fc-20261126-35": "SC Freiburg are 14 with 6 points; FC Twente are 3 with 9 points. Recent official five-game records: home 5W/0D/0L, scoring 9 and conceding 3; away 4W/1D/0L, scoring 18 and conceding 4. Freiburg have won five straight games, but Twente are also unbeaten in five. The visitors’ scoring record gives them a way to respond to home pressure. Their ability to remain competitive supports Twente in a difficult fixture. FC Twente is my selection.", "fc-20261126-36": "Braga are 17 with 4 points; KuPS Kuopio are 33 with 1 points. Available European-only records are used for KuPS Kuopio. Recent official five-game records: home 3W/1D/1L, scoring 6 and conceding 1; away 1W/2D/2L, scoring 4 and conceding 7. Braga have controlled concessions in recent games and can manage the tempo. KuPS may regroup behind the ball and reduce space away from home. Home game management and visiting defensive emphasis support a more restrained scoring contest. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261127-01": "Forest are 17th on nine points, but their home win over Manchester City shows they can raise their level. Chelsea are eighth on sixteen points yet have lost their last two league matches, conceding four against Leeds. Caicedo is available again, while Forest welcome Hudson-Odoi back. Chelsea possess attacking quality, but their defensive uncertainty leaves room for the hosts to press the issue. Forest are the selection.", "fc-20261127-02": "Venezia are bottom with six points and have lost four of their last five without scoring. Their home win over Udinese offers encouragement, but Bologna bring a more sustained improvement: four wins and a draw in five, scoring in every game. Bologna are ninth with eighteen points and their varied attack can keep Venezia under pressure. Bologna are the selection.", "fc-20261127-03": "Levante have drawn their last two league games but continue to struggle for goals. Racing are seventh with seventeen points after consecutive wins over Malaga and Real Sociedad. Their defence remains vulnerable, so this is no straightforward away assignment, but their recent finishing gives them a credible route through Levante. Racing are the selection.", "fc-20261127-04": "Bremen are sixth on eighteen points after beating Hamburg without conceding. Their recent home win over Hoffenheim also shows a useful balance between attacking pressure and defensive control. Gladbach are bottom on four points and have conceded twenty-six goals in ten league games. Bremen have shown inconsistency away, but the current home attacking rhythm gives them the stronger case. Bremen are the selection.", "fc-20261127-05": "Paris FC are second on twenty-three points with four wins in five, yet Brest present a serious obstacle. The hosts are sixth on eighteen points and have won three straight league games without conceding. That organisation can deny Paris the space enjoyed in recent victories. With home advantage and a settled defensive rhythm, Brest are the selection.", "fc-20261127-06": "Middlesbrough lead the Championship with thirty-five points after consecutive wins, but Southampton remain unbeaten at St Marys. Saints are sixth on twenty-eight points after their four-point deduction and their home attack has been productive. Boro carry a genuine scoring threat, but Southampton can sustain pressure of their own. Southampton are the selection.", "fc-20261127-07": "Heidenheim are seventh on sixteen points but have failed to win in five and conceded in every game. Nuremberg are second on twenty-four points with twenty-seven league goals. Their latest defeat shows they also have vulnerabilities, yet the visitors have a stronger season-long balance and can test a fragile home defence. Nuremberg are the selection.", "fc-20261127-08": "Bochum had won three straight competitive games before losing at St Pauli, but their season total of eleven league goals limits the case for a dominant display. Darmstadt have lost only once in five and arrive after scoring three against Heidenheim. Their recent improvement gives them a route to a close contest despite a low table position. Darmstadt are the selection.", "fc-20261127-09": "Groningen have scored thirty league goals but their last five matches brought fourteen conceded. Willem II remain without a league win and have conceded forty-two in thirteen games, although they scored in their last two. Groningen can create chances, while their own defensive gaps offer the visitors opportunities. Over is the selection.", "fc-20261127-10": "Sonderjyske have conceded at least twice in each of their last four games. Brondby have failed to score in two successive defeats and need to recover their attacking rhythm. The hosts can also contribute chances, having scored twenty league goals. With both sides needing a response and defensive space likely to emerge, Over is the selection.", "fc-20261127-11": "Maritimo have failed to score in three successive competitive matches. Nacional have won two of their last three, but each of those three games was decided by a single goal. The home side need control after defensive problems, while Nacional have not shown a prolific attack. A cautious contest is plausible; Under is the selection.", "fc-20261127-12": "Leuven had gone four games unbeaten before losing at Anderlecht. Kortrijk are bottom with four points and have scored just four league goals in twelve games. The hosts also average only one league goal per game, while Kortrijk conceded only once in each of their last two defeats. The attacking limitations make Under the selection.", "fc-20261127-13": "Leganes have won three straight competitive games, scoring three in each of their last two league matches. Sabadell sit one point higher but have gone four league games without a victory and rely heavily on draws. The visitors can make this awkward, but the hosts current chance conversion and home pressure give Leganes the edge. Leganes are the selection."});
Object.assign(E.summary,{"fc-20261123-01": "Thiago's suspension and injuries to Hickey and Collins weaken Brentford at both ends. Everton arrive with three consecutive wins and Barry in scoring form. Their momentum and fuller squad make Everton the selection.", "fc-20261123-02": "Monza have lost four straight games and remain defensively unsettled. Fiorentina have taken points against Atalanta and Juventus around an away win over Sassuolo. Their improvement makes Fiorentina the selection.", "fc-20261123-03": "Only one point separates these relegation-zone sides, and Elche's away resilience deserves respect. Levante have earned both league wins at home. That home attacking potential gives Levante a narrow edge.", "fc-20261120-01": "Espanyol's last two clean sheets demand patient attacking play. Athletic have won three of five competitive matches and hold the stronger league position, giving the hosts the edge at San Mames. Athletic need patient possession to draw Espanyol out of their defensive shape. Athletic Club are my selection.", "fc-20261120-02": "Cologne are winless in four league matches and have struggled away. Despite several injuries, Bayern's unbeaten league record, powerful home attack and Kompany's return strongly favour the hosts. Bayern can strengthen their control by restricting Cologne early in possession. Bayern Munich are my selection.", "fc-20261120-03": "Le Havre's five straight defeats and winless league campaign expose a vulnerable defence. Troyes also struggle to score but have shown an ability to keep clean sheets and can make home advantage count. Troyes need to wait for defensive errors without opening up their own back line. Troyes are my selection.", "fc-20261120-04": "Magdeburg carry a dangerous attack and sit three points higher. Bielefeld's successive league wins provide a steadier platform, and disciplined midfield play can help the hosts make home advantage count. Bielefeld must limit Magdeburg in midfield during attacking transitions. Arminia Bielefeld are my selection.", "fc-20261120-05": "Heidenheim's five-match winless sequence limits confidence. Darmstadt face problems at both ends near the bottom, however, leaving the visitors with a narrow advantage based on their stronger season record. Space conceded by Darmstadt could help Heidenheim return to winning ways. 1. FC Heidenheim 1846 are my selection.", "fc-20261120-06": "Molde's scoring power comes with defensive exposure. Bodo/Glimt have won successive league matches and hold a considerably stronger season record, giving them the edge in an open contest. Molde must avoid leaving Bodo/Glimt large spaces in an exchange of attacks. Bodo/Glimt are my selection.", "fc-20261120-07": "Lyngby can threaten on the counter but have lost three of five. AGF's latest league win came with a clean sheet, and their more controlled recent performances favour the home side. AGF can gain greater control by closing Lyngby's counterattacking routes. AGF are my selection.", "fc-20261120-08": "Westerlo retain attacking ability but have conceded heavily in successive defeats. Cercle's two straight wins, including a clean sheet last time, give the hosts a platform to exploit that defensive weakness. Cercle should press Westerlo without the ball and exploit defensive errors. Cercle Brugge KSV are my selection.", "fc-20261120-09": "Only one point separates these teams despite their different positions. Cesena are competitive, but Verona's three straight clean sheets and five-match unbeaten run give the hosts the stronger foundation. Verona can seek a narrow result if they contain Cesena's responses. Hellas Verona are my selection.", "fc-20261120-10": "Andorra continue to struggle for league points and defensive stability. Leganes are also vulnerable at the back but consecutive cup and league victories give the visitors a narrow recent-form edge. Andorra need better defensive connections to stop Leganes building on their recent wins. Leganés are my selection.", "fc-20261120-11": "Annecy's penalty-shootout cup advancement does not erase two heavy league defeats. Clermont's latest league win came with a clean sheet, giving the lower-ranked visitors an opportunity to take a result. Annecy must first reduce their concessions against an improving Clermont attack. Clermont Foot are my selection.", "fc-20261120-12": "Both sides have recent weaknesses and only one point separates them. Guingamp's clean-sheet wins before their latest league setback, together with home advantage, provide a small edge. Guingamp should close Rodez's counterattacking routes while building home pressure. Guingamp are my selection.", "fc-20261120-13": "Boulogne's many league draws call for patience from Metz. Both teams won their latest league games, but the hosts' attacking display at Montpellier and home advantage give them a slight edge. Metz need patience against Boulogne and precision when clear opportunities arrive. Metz are my selection.", "fc-20261120-14": "Dijon's successive league wins deserve respect. Nancy nevertheless have four straight league victories and a stronger defensive platform, making the second-placed hosts the more convincing choice. Nancy can build on their league sequence by denying Dijon midfield space. AS Nancy Lorraine are my selection.", "fc-20261120-15": "Red Star's cup success sits alongside four straight league defeats. Pau have won three of their last four league games and added a convincing cup victory, providing the stronger recent platform. Red Star must protect the spaces lost in transition, but Pau's recent league record is stronger. Pau are my selection.", "fc-20261121-01": "City must respond to three successive league defeats. Their five competitive games brought ten goals conceded, while Fulham conceded only three in five and drew with Newcastle last time. Maresca's confirmation that Marc Guehi is available helps the hosts, but patience and defensive balance remain essential. Home advantage and their chance creation give Manchester City a narrow preference.", "fc-20261121-02": "Villa's 4-4 draw at United showed attacking promise and serious defensive problems. They have only one win in five, while Sunderland arrive after beating Chelsea without conceding. The visitors deserve respect, but Villa's attacking response and home advantage give the hosts a cautious preference.", "fc-20261121-03": "Bournemouth have won five competitive games in a row, scoring 13 and conceding two. Forest's win over City is a warning against complacency, but the hosts have the more sustained record. Scott and Kroupi's availability helps Marco Rose, while Forest lack Hudson-Odoi. Bournemouth are the selection.", "fc-20261121-04": "Chelsea need sharper finishing after losing to Sunderland; their last five brought only five goals. Leeds beat Tottenham but scored just three in five themselves. Caicedo is available, although Chelsea retain several absences. A tight contest is likely, with home advantage favouring Chelsea.", "fc-20261121-05": "Both clubs are near the bottom. Coventry scored and conceded nine in five, while Palace scored only three. Thomas Frank's first match may bring a response, but Mateta's suspension and Sarr's injury limit the visitors. Coventry's greater recent attacking output and home advantage earn a narrow preference.", "fc-20261121-06": "Tottenham's defeat at Leeds followed three consecutive wins and should not erase their defensive improvement: only three conceded in five. Ipswich have gone four without a win. Savio and Bergvall are available again, although Tel remains out. Tottenham's stronger balance at home makes them the selection.", "fc-20261121-07": "Newcastle have only one win in five. Arsenal lead with 27 points and conceded only twice in their last five competitive games. Saliba is available again, but Zubimendi and Saka are out. The hosts can make this uncomfortable, yet Arsenal's defensive consistency makes them the selection.", "fc-20261121-08": "Como's loss to Inter ended four straight wins; they still scored 15 in five. Cagliari stopped four defeats by beating Frosinone, but conceded 12 across that five-game run. Como's stronger attacking record and home advantage make them the selection.", "fc-20261121-09": "Lazio remain top on 29 points after drawing with Napoli, with four wins and a draw in five and 14 goals scored. Lecce stopped three defeats by drawing with Torino but remain winless in four. The hosts' consistency and attacking output favour Lazio.", "fc-20261121-10": "Parma have only one win in five and eight league points. Roma beat Sassuolo without conceding and scored 17 in five, although ten conceded show that their defence is not secure. Their greater attacking threat and third-place standing give Roma the preference.", "fc-20261121-11": "Only one point separates these teams, and both are winless in three. Napoli's draw with leaders Lazio was encouraging, although 11 conceded in five remain a concern. Torino have also struggled for consistency. Napoli receive a narrow home preference rather than a strong endorsement.", "fc-20261121-12": "Alaves' six-goal cup win should not erase the four winless matches before it. Deportivo are unbeaten in three and conceded only three in five. With the visitors ninth on 15 points and more defensively reliable, Deportivo receive a cautious preference.", "fc-20261121-13": "Rayo's defeat at Sociedad followed two wins. Valencia's six-goal cup success should be distinguished from their league defeat by Real Madrid and 19th-place position. Rayo have the modest table advantage and play at home, earning a cautious preference.", "fc-20261121-14": "Derby intensity reduces the value of table position alone. Sevilla are winless in two, while Betis have won twice and sit eight points ahead. Betis must avoid the defensive lapses seen in their cup game, but recent consistency gives the visitors the preference.", "fc-20261121-15": "Madrid have won five competitive games in a row, scoring 15, and beat Valencia without conceding. Celta's five-goal cup victory followed four winless matches and came in a different competitive context. Madrid's more sustained record and home advantage make them the selection.", "fc-20261121-16": "Leverkusen ended two defeats by beating Cologne, but 11 conceded in five show continuing defensive risk. Paderborn's draw with Frankfurt merits respect; friendly results are excluded from the competitive assessment. Leverkusen receive a home preference, provided they protect space behind their attacks.", "fc-20261121-17": "Gladbach's friendly win is excluded from the competitive assessment. Their four league points and bottom position contrast with Dortmund's 21 points and unbeaten five-match competitive run. The visitors still concede chances, but Dortmund's more consistent results make them the selection.", "fc-20261121-18": "Both teams have 12 points and conceded five in their last five. Frankfurt are unbeaten in three, while Hoffenheim responded by beating Schalke but remain inconsistent. The margins look small; Frankfurt's recent continuity and home advantage earn a narrow preference.", "fc-20261121-19": "Elversberg remain a credible home opponent but conceded 12 in five. Freiburg have won four in a row and kept a clean sheet against Union. The hosts can score, yet Freiburg's stronger recent balance makes the visitors the selection.", "fc-20261121-20": "Union's seven league points and limited scoring are concerns after their goalless defeat at Wolfsburg. Leipzig's friendly is excluded from the assessment; their fourth place and 18 points provide the stronger competitive basis. Leipzig are preferred, with defensive concentration still essential away from home.", "fc-20261121-21": "Schalke have lost three straight and scored once in five. Stuttgart arrive after a clean-sheet win over Bremen and have three wins in five. Away inconsistency remains a risk, but the hosts' limited scoring makes Stuttgart the preference.", "fc-20261121-22": "Nice have won three straight and scored 12 in five, so this is a real test. PSG have won all five, scoring 18 and conceding three. Both can threaten, but PSG's stronger balance at both ends gives the league leaders the preference.", "fc-20261121-23": "Monaco are unbeaten in two and have the stronger league position. Auxerre have lost twice in a row and conceded 12 in five. The visitors can slow the game, but Monaco's more stable record and home advantage make them the selection.", "fc-20261121-24": "Lille are unbeaten in three after beating Rennes and sit second on 21 points. Lyon are fifth but scored only three in five and lost without scoring at Brest. With chances potentially scarce, Lille's recent stability at home gives them the preference.", "fc-20261121-25": "Both clubs have 13 points, but Lens have lost three straight and conceded 16 in five. Toulouse beat Strasbourg and conceded only five across their last five. The hosts can respond, yet the visitors' defensive balance gives Toulouse a cautious preference.", "fc-20261121-26": "Strasbourg have lost four of five and conceded 12. Brest have won their last two, most recently without conceding against Lyon, and scored 11 while allowing four in five. The visitors' stronger form at both ends makes Brest the selection.", "fc-20261121-27": "Norwich's five-goal win over Bristol City extended a four-match winning run. Cardiff scored five against Burnley but conceded four, illustrating their defensive risk. Norwich's better recent balance and home advantage make them the selection.", "fc-20261121-28": "Millwall have lost their last two, most recently without scoring at West Brom. QPR beat Lincoln and are unbeaten in two, although nine conceded in five reveal defensive risk. Their stronger table position and recent response earn QPR a cautious preference.", "fc-20261121-29": "Southampton's defeat to Preston was poor, but it followed four unbeaten games. Derby ended four winless matches by beating Bolton, yet remain 23rd with ten points and 11 conceded in five. The hosts' stronger overall balance favours Southampton.", "fc-20261121-30": "Portsmouth's loss to Stoke followed four unbeaten matches. Bolton have only one win in five and conceded 11, compared with Portsmouth's five. Home pressure is a factor, but the visitors' stronger defensive continuity makes Portsmouth the selection.", "fc-20261121-31": "Both sides have 29 points and three successive wins. Stoke conceded only two in five; Birmingham scored 11 while conceding three. This is a close contest between strong teams. Birmingham receive only a marginal preference for their greater attacking output.", "fc-20261121-32": "Lincoln have lost three straight. Wrexham drew with Wolves and are unbeaten in two, conceding only five in their last five. The hosts urgently need points, but urgency does not remove their defensive problems. Wrexham's better balance earns a cautious preference.", "fc-20261121-33": "Swansea sit sixth but have lost four of five and conceded 11. West Brom are unbeaten in five, scoring 11 and most recently beating Millwall without conceding. The table gap is small; the form gap favours West Brom.", "fc-20261121-34": "Middlesbrough are second with 29 points and scored ten in five, despite going winless in their last two. Bristol City arrive after a five-goal loss to Norwich and two straight defeats. The hosts' stronger attacking base and home advantage favour Middlesbrough.", "fc-20261121-35": "West Ham are winless in four and cannot treat the bottom club lightly. Preston beat Southampton without conceding, but that followed four winless games and they still have only eight points. Both carry risk; West Ham receive a cautious home preference.", "fc-20261121-36": "Wolves are unbeaten in five and conceded only three, holding fourth place on 28 points. Charlton's win over Sheffield United ended four defeats but does not erase ten conceded in five. Wolves' sustained defensive and results record makes them the selection.", "fc-20261121-37": "Sheffield United's loss to Charlton ended four unbeaten games. Watford held Middlesbrough goalless and conceded only four in five, so the hosts may need patience. Sheffield United's three wins in five and home advantage earn a narrow preference.", "fc-20261116-01": "Netherlands arrive in Berlin unbeaten in five after scoring seven against Greece. Germany regained confidence with an away win over Serbia, but are third on eight points and urgently need a home result. Containing Dutch transitions is crucial; **Germany are my selection.**", "fc-20261116-02": "Serbia have lost every group fixture, while Greece remain second with eight points. The heavy defeat in the Netherlands will test Greece's confidence, but their preceding four-match unbeaten run and home advantage favour **Greece.**", "fc-20261116-03": "North Macedonia have lost five straight and failed to score in both home matches. Slovenia have eight points, held Switzerland scoreless and won away to Scotland. Their more stable performances make **Slovenia my selection.**", "fc-20261116-04": "Scotland arrive after a win, but Switzerland remain unbeaten with four victories from five and have won both home fixtures. Their superior group form and home strength favour **Switzerland.**", "fc-20261116-05": "Moldova are two points ahead, so the Faroe Islands need a victory rather than a sixth consecutive draw. Their unbeaten resistance and home motivation give **Faroe Islands my selection.**", "fc-20261116-06": "Slovakia lead with three wins and two draws; Kazakhstan remain winless. The visitors also scored four away to Moldova. Recent attacking efficiency and group form favour **Slovakia.**", "fc-20261116-07": "Estonia have kept four straight clean sheets and remain unbeaten on nine points, while Bulgaria conceded five in their latest game. Defensive stability and home advantage make **Estonia my selection.**", "fc-20261116-08": "Luxembourg have lost four in a row and failed to score in their last three. Iceland lead with eleven points, four successive clean sheets and five goals in their latest win. **Iceland are my selection.**", "fc-20261116-09": "Liechtenstein have not scored in five games. Lithuania failed to score in their latest friendly but recently netted three at home against Andorra. A patient approach favours **Lithuania.**", "fc-20261116-10": "Malta have three wins and two draws from their last five; Gibraltar lost to Andorra without scoring. Gibraltar drew in Malta, but the visitors' stronger form makes **Malta my selection.**", "fc-20261116-11": "Celta Fortuna are winless in four and lost consecutive away games. Albacete have won three straight league fixtures and another cup match. Their improving finishing and home edge make **Albacete my selection.**", "fc-20261122-01": "Hull have resisted opponents but remain winless in five. Brighton have three consecutive clean-sheet victories and sit second. Their greater defensive stability makes Brighton the selection.", "fc-20261122-02": "Pochettino starts United life at Anfield with major defensive problems to solve. Liverpool have recovered at Palace and have more players returning to training. Liverpool are the selection.", "fc-20261122-03": "Venezia won last time but have lost nine league games and their last two away outings without scoring. Juventus are unbeaten in three and can sustain home pressure. Juventus are the selection.", "fc-20261122-04": "Udinese have failed to score in four of five games and remain bottom. Bologna have won their last four league fixtures. The improving home side are the selection.", "fc-20261122-05": "Sassuolo have conceded 19 goals in five matches and lost four in a row. Genoa are also vulnerable but possess the stronger recent base. Genoa are the selection.", "fc-20261122-06": "Frosinone can score and are close to Milan in the table, so this is no routine home fixture. Milan retain the stronger opportunity to decide the contest at San Siro. Milan are the selection.", "fc-20261122-07": "Atalanta can threaten but have conceded ten goals in five. Inter have won four of five with three clean sheets, offering the better balance. Inter are the selection.", "fc-20261122-08": "Villarreal beat Getafe without conceding last time but lost at home to Espanyol in their previous league match, but Barcelona offer a different attacking test. Despite defensive absences, the leaders have more options returning. Barcelona are the selection.", "fc-20261122-09": "Racing have recovered some confidence, while Sociedad must improve on their last away league defeat. The visitors still have the stronger form and league position. Sociedad are the selection.", "fc-20261122-10": "Malaga remain winless after twelve league fixtures. Osasuna should not overvalue a lower-level cup win, but their recent home draw with Athletic offers a firmer basis. Osasuna are the selection.", "fc-20261122-11": "Getafe can resist at home but have had scoreless losses against stronger sides. Atletico had two clean-sheet league wins before consecutive defeats to Bayern and Barcelona. Atletico are the selection.", "fc-20261122-12": "Only one point separates these vulnerable teams. Augsburg conceded five last time, creating a narrow opportunity for Mainz despite the visitors own problems. Mainz are the selection.", "fc-20261122-13": "Hamburg arrive after a confidence-building win, but the derby creates a tougher away test. Werder have home advantage and continuity under Thioune. Werder are the selection.", "fc-20261122-14": "Paris FC have beaten Monaco and Rennes at home and remain near the top. Angers are winless in five with limited attacking output. Paris FC are the selection.", "fc-20261122-15": "These teams are separated by one point and both have recent weaknesses. Lorient lost their latest home game after winning their preceding two, while Rennes retain a useful attacking threat. Rennes are the selection.", "fc-20261122-16": "Le Mans can frustrate but have struggled to win. Marseille have four victories in five, including important recent away successes, and can sustain home pressure. Marseille are the selection.", "fc-20261122-17": "Burnley are winless in five despite home derby motivation. Blackburn have won two of five, though their away losses require caution. Blackburn are the selection.", "fc-20261122-18": "Cottbus have drawn often but won none of five. Hertha remain unbeaten in the league and have shown strong away form at Kaiserslautern. Hertha are the selection.", "fc-20261122-19": "Dresden won convincingly last time but have recent away defeats. Kaiserslautern have four wins and four clean sheets in five. The home side are the selection.", "fc-20261122-20": "Both have eleven points and neither is consistent. Karlsruhe have won their last two at home, while Osnabruck have only one victory in five. Karlsruhe are the selection.", "fc-20261124-01": "Bodø/Glimt sit 25th with four points from four Champions League matches and have conceded more than they have scored. LASK are 16th on six points after consecutive wins in the competition. Although Bodø/Glimt have home advantage, LASK's recent form suggests that a heavy defeat is unlikely. **LASK are my selection.**", "fc-20261124-02": "Galatasaray sit 18th with six points after consecutive Champions League victories. Unai Emery's Aston Villa are sixth on nine points and have been strong in attack. However, Villa may find it difficult to attack freely at Galatasaray's ground, and both sides may prioritise securing points. **Under is my selection.**", "fc-20261124-03": "Arteta's Arsenal remain unbeaten in the Champions League, sitting third with ten points. Their defensive stability is a key strength, but Dortmund have also won three of four games. Arsenal may have the advantage at home, yet beating Dortmund by a large margin will not be easy. **Dortmund are my selection.**", "fc-20261124-04": "Como have impressed in attack in this season's Champions League. Douvikas's finishing and Nico Paz's creativity could cause difficulties for AEK Athens' defence. AEK have defensive weaknesses but can score in reply. **Over is my selection.**", "fc-20261124-05": "Feyenoord and Porto have only three Champions League points each, so both need a win. Feyenoord have been conceding frequently, while Porto have gained confidence in attack. Both sides could open up in search of victory and have defensive weaknesses. **Over is my selection.**", "fc-20261124-06": "Manchester City have scored 12 goals in four Champions League games and sit seventh with nine points. Napoli have conceded frequently and could struggle to contain an attack led by Haaland. Napoli also have attacking quality through De Bruyne, McTominay and Højlund, so both teams could score. **Over is my selection.**", "fc-20261124-07": "Leipzig and Lens have struggled for Champions League results, but Lens's defensive weaknesses are more pronounced. Leipzig can score and should be able to put Lens under pressure at home. Given Lens's defensive and away difficulties, **Leipzig are my selection.**", "fc-20261124-08": "Real Madrid have won all four Champions League games and possess a strong attack. PSV, however, can defend in an organised manner and make life difficult for Madrid. Madrid may win, but a wide winning margin will not be easy. **PSV are my selection.**", "fc-20261124-09": "Slovan Bratislava have lost all four Champions League matches and struggled in both attack and defence. Real Betis have nine points, and Isco and Antony's creativity could threaten Slovan's back line. The difference in form suggests a sizeable winning margin is possible. **Real Betis are my selection.**", "fc-20261124-10": "Bristol City are 18th on 18 points and have won only one of their last five games, struggling for results at home. Wrexham are 14th on 21 points and unbeaten in three. Comparing their recent form and consistency, **Wrexham are my selection.**", "fc-20261124-11": "Cardiff are unbeaten in eight home matches this season and have secured good home results. Preston sit bottom on nine points and have conceded frequently. Weighing Cardiff's home form against Preston's weaknesses, **Cardiff are my selection.**", "fc-20261124-12": "Charlton and Lincoln sit near the bottom of the table and have each lost four of their last five. Both struggle to finish chances and may play cautiously to avoid losing points near the relegation zone. With both attacks struggling, **Under is my selection.**", "fc-20261124-13": "Middlesbrough lead the table with 32 points and 32 goals in 16 games, and remain unbeaten at home. Swansea's recent results have dipped, but they retain the ability to score. Given Middlesbrough's home scoring and Swansea's ability to respond, **Over is my selection.**", "fc-20261124-14": "Norwich have won five consecutive league matches and are in strong attacking form. QPR sit seventh and have lost only one of their last five. With both sides in good form and possessing attacking quality, both could score. **Over is my selection.**", "fc-20261124-15": "Portsmouth have lost only one of their last five and have been consistent. West Ham possess attacking quality but have gone five games without a win. Although West Ham have the stronger squad, Portsmouth's recent form and home advantage make them appealing. **Portsmouth are my selection.**", "fc-20261124-16": "Sheffield United sit ninth on 25 points, while Southampton are sixth on 27. Southampton's defensive stability may make it difficult for Sheffield United to score, but the hosts will not give in easily at home. In a closely matched contest, **Under is my selection.**", "fc-20261124-17": "Wolves sit third on 31 points and have won four and drawn one of their last five. Derby are 23rd on ten points, weak in attack and conceding frequently. Wolves' current form and home attack suggest that a wide winning margin is possible. **Wolves are my selection.**", "fc-20261125-01": "Sabah have three points from four European matches and must protect their defensive shape after a heavy defeat at Viking. Barcelona arrive with four consecutive wins, including their latest success against Villarreal. Hansi Flick's side should control possession; Sabah's counterattacks remain a threat, but Barcelona's attacking quality makes them the selection.", "fc-20261125-02": "Slavia have won their last two domestic matches but have one point and Villarreal three after four Champions League games. Villarreal's heavy loss to PSG exposed their defence, but scoring twice against Barcelona showed their attacking threat. Slavia's home pressure could leave openings, so Villarreal are the selection in a difficult contest.", "fc-20261125-03": "Atlético and Viking both have four European points. Viking's draw with Bayern and win over Sabah underline their attacking threat, although their latest domestic defeat is a concern. Atlético recovered with a clean-sheet win over Getafe and should control more of this home match. Atlético are the selection.", "fc-20261125-04": "Both clubs have nine European points. Brugge are unbeaten in five and arrive after a large win at Mechelen, while Liverpool's convincing victory over Manchester United has restored attacking confidence. The visitors must avoid the defensive lapses seen at Fenerbahce, but their threat in open spaces makes Liverpool the selection.", "fc-20261125-05": "Inter have six European points, one fewer than Stuttgart. Their four-goal draw with Atalanta showed both attacking strength and defensive vulnerability. Stuttgart have kept clean sheets in their last two matches but lost their previous European away game at Galatasaray. Inter's home advantage and attacking options make them the selection.", "fc-20261125-06": "Lille have only one European point and failed to score in their latest defeat to Lyon. Bayern remain unbeaten in the competition and in their last five matches, including a European away win at Atlético. Lille may keep the game tight, but Bayern have more ways to create the decisive chance and are the selection.", "fc-20261125-07": "PSG have won all four European matches and their last five fixtures. Roma bring strong attacking form of their own after a convincing win over Parma, but have only four European points and conceded three at Manchester United. PSG must stay alert to transitions; their home pressure and chance creation still make them the selection.", "fc-20261125-08": "Shakhtar have failed to score in their last two European defeats. Fenerbahce's win over Liverpool showed greater attacking potential, although their latest domestic draw exposed defensive weaknesses. The visitors must be patient against a compact opponent, but Fenerbahce are the selection for their stronger recent European attacking display.", "fc-20261125-09": "Sporting have four consecutive clean-sheet wins and nine European points. Manchester United arrive after a heavy defeat at Liverpool, leaving Mauricio Pochettino with immediate defensive work. Their comeback against Roma shows attacking potential, but Sporting's organisation and home advantage make the Portuguese side the selection.", "fc-20261125-10": "Bolton are nineteenth with 18 points and have won only once in five. Fifth-placed West Brom have 29 points and are unbeaten in five, with wins over Millwall and West Ham. Their tendency to draw means patience is needed, but Bolton's defensive problems make West Brom the selection.", "fc-20261125-11": "Burnley have one win from sixteen league games and none in their last five. Birmingham remain fourth with 29 points despite losing at Stoke, following three consecutive wins. Burnley's draws make this awkward, but Birmingham's stronger season and recent performances make them the selection.", "fc-20261125-12": "Watford's heavy defeat at Sheffield United and limited recent scoring undermine their home advantage. Blackburn also concede too often, but are unbeaten in two after beating West Ham. The game could remain close for long spells; Blackburn's more convincing recent goal threat makes them the selection.", "fc-20261125-13": "Stoke are third with 32 points and four consecutive wins, most recently a clean-sheet victory over Birmingham. Millwall have lost three in a row without scoring. They may defend deep and rely on set pieces, but Stoke's confidence and ability to sustain pressure make the home side the selection.", "fc-20261125-14": "Cremonese need to respond after losing at Südtirol, which ended a three-match winning run. Fifth-placed Avellino are unbeaten in four and arrive after a convincing victory over Mantova. Cremonese can press at home, but Avellino's current resilience and attacking confidence make the visitors the selection.", "fc-20261125-15": "Mantova are seventh but winless in four after a heavy defeat to Avellino. Arezzo have also struggled, with no wins and three defeats in their last five. Neither attack offers strong certainty; Mantova must rebuild their defensive confidence, but home advantage gives them the edge and makes them the selection.", "fc-20261125-16": "Padova are unbeaten in five but have drawn their last three. Sampdoria have won three in succession, conceding only once in those victories. The hosts should make this competitive, yet Sampdoria's sharper recent finishing and improved defensive results make them the selection.", "fc-20261125-17": "Pisa ended a four-game winless run by beating Empoli. Modena, second with 26 points, have four wins and a draw in five and clean sheets in their last two. Pisa's home advantage matters, but Modena's more consistent defending and attacking returns make them the selection.", "fc-20261126-02": "Celta Vigo vs AFC Bournemouth. Celta are without injured Borja Iglesias, Carl Starfelt and Miguel Roman, reducing options in both attack and defence. Bournemouth’s five consecutive wins and limited concessions provide a more stable foundation. They can look to exploit space when Celta push forward. AFC Bournemouth is my selection.", "fc-20261126-04": "Olympiacos vs AC Milan. Olympiacos can apply pressure at home, while Milan have attacking confidence after scoring five against Frosinone. Amorim nevertheless acknowledges that Milan’s defending needs improvement. The attacking output and need for points suggest chances at both ends. Over is my selection.", "fc-20261126-09": "Crystal Palace vs Real Sociedad. Palace are developing Thomas Frank’s approach, while Sociedad’s recent results are also mixed. Equal European points give both sides reason to avoid costly errors. A contested midfield and fewer clear chances support a restrained game. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261126-01": "Besiktas vs Hapoel Be'er. Besiktas have shown sustained scoring ability and can seek to dictate the tempo at home. Hapoel’s available European records show frequent concessions, making prolonged home pressure a concern. Converting early chances would allow the hosts to maintain control. Besiktas is my selection.", "fc-20261126-03": "Dinamo Zagreb vs Bayer Leverkusen. Dinamo can try to raise the tempo at home but must contain Leverkusen’s recent scoring output. The visitors arrive after consecutive wins and have regained attacking rhythm. Their combination play and ability to convert chances support the selection. Bayer Leverkusen is my selection.", "fc-20261126-05": "Marseille vs Levski Sofia. Marseille’s latest defeat followed four straight wins, so one result does not erase that earlier progress. Levski have collected European points and should not be dismissed. The hosts’ pressure and recent scoring ability remain persuasive. Marseille is my selection.", "fc-20261126-06": "RB Salzburg vs Ararat-Armenia. Salzburg retain an attacking foundation despite losing their latest match. Ararat-Armenia’s concessions in the available official records offer an opening. Maintaining discipline after turnovers would help the hosts sustain control. RB Salzburg is my selection.", "fc-20261126-07": "Union St.-Gilloise vs Lech Poznan. Union have won five straight games and limited concessions in their latest fixtures. Lech have struggled for victories in the available official records. The combination of attacking momentum and defensive stability favours the hosts. Union St.-Gilloise is my selection.", "fc-20261126-08": "Viktoria Plzen vs Benfica. Benfica have won five straight matches, but Plzen can seek to reduce space at home. The visitors may control possession patiently when ahead. A cautious home approach and controlled visiting play support a more restrained scoring contest. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261126-10": "Ferencvaros vs NK Celje. Ferencvaros have sustained a winning run both recently and in the Europa League. Celje’s recent defeats may affect confidence. Early home pressure and the ability to maintain attacking rhythm support Ferencvaros. Ferencvaros is my selection.", "fc-20261126-11": "Juventus vs Omonia Nicosia. Juventus can expect more possession, while Omonia may prioritise closing space after consecutive defeats. Defensive discipline should be important to the visitors. Home control, rather than an uncontrolled exchange, supports a lower-scoring assessment. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261126-12": "NEC Nijmegen vs Stade Rennais. NEC and Rennes have inconsistent recent records, encouraging an emphasis on avoiding errors. Rennes need to reorganise quickly after losing possession away from home. Midfield contests and defensive obstruction may outweigh clean finishing opportunities. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261126-13": "OFI Crete vs Anderlecht. Crete and Anderlecht have equal European points, making this difficult to separate. The hosts can try to close space and disrupt the visitors’ combinations. Protecting points could lead to fewer openings. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261126-14": "Lyon vs Lillestrom. Lyon have the stronger European position, but Lillestrom’s recent victories deserve respect. The visitors can defend patiently and choose their moments. Home possession control and visiting caution support a restrained contest. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261126-15": "Torreense vs Celtic. Celtic arrive after three consecutive wins and with greater confidence. Torreense still struggle to reproduce positive results consistently. The visitors’ ability to convert their opportunities supports Celtic. Celtic is my selection.", "fc-20261126-16": "Sparta Prague vs AZ Alkmaar. Sparta and AZ have not provided a consistently dependable defensive picture. Both need European points and may have to take the initiative. More transitions from midfield into attack could create scoring opportunities. Over is my selection.", "fc-20261126-17": "Sunderland vs Jagiellonia Bialystok. Sunderland’s recent results do not establish a consistently reliable attack. Jagiellonia can try to reduce the tempo and deny space. The available European records and finishing patterns favour caution over a free-scoring exchange. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261126-18": "TSG Hoffenheim vs SK Sturm Graz. Hoffenheim and Sturm have equal European points and need a win. Their recent records do not establish a dependable attacking advantage. A cautious start could leave midfield contests more prominent than clear chances. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261126-19": "Kairat Almaty vs Mjällby AIF. Kairat are winless in five while Mjallby are unbeaten over the same span. Home support can lift the tempo, but wasted chances may increase pressure on Kairat. The visitors’ resilience supports the selection. Mjällby AIF is my selection.", "fc-20261126-20": "Ajax Amsterdam vs FC Thun. Ajax have won frequently and can seek possession control at home. Thun may defend compactly rather than open the game immediately. If the hosts manage a lead patiently, an end-to-end attacking contest need not develop. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261126-21": "SK Brann vs AGF. Brann and AGF show limited recent separation, with draws in their records. Both need to restrict space after losing the ball. A game built around waiting for mistakes could be more cautious than open. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261126-22": "Brighton & Hove Albion vs CSU Craiova. Brighton and Craiova have equal European points, so the visitors deserve respect. Regrouping behind the ball could force the hosts to build attacks patiently. Possession control need not turn this into a wide-open game. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261126-23": "Egnatia vs Lincoln Red Imps. Egnatia’s five-game winless sequence raises questions about attacking confidence. Lincoln can prioritise closing space away from home. Recent scoring output and cautious game management support fewer clear openings. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261126-24": "Jablonec vs FC Lugano. Lugano have won all three European games, while Jablonec have struggled for points. That record provides confidence in the visitors’ approach. Patience under home pressure and better use of chances support Lugano. FC Lugano is my selection.", "fc-20261126-25": "Heart of Midlothian vs AS Monaco. Hearts need points at home, and Monaco’s recent record does not establish complete defensive reliability. Both may commit players when attacking opportunities arise. Changes in momentum and chances at either end support goals. Over is my selection.", "fc-20261126-26": "Iberia 1999 vs Getafe. Iberia have struggled for wins, while Getafe’s recent results also raise questions about attacking consistency. Both need organisation and defensive recovery to avoid an early setback. Contested possession may outweigh precise finishing. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261126-27": "Kauno Zalgiris vs Riga FC. Zalgiris have lost their latest three games, while Riga are unbeaten in the five available official records. Frequent home concessions offer opportunities to the visitors. Riga’s ability to remain competitive under pressure supports the selection. Riga FC is my selection.", "fc-20261126-28": "Pafos vs FC Midtjylland. Pafos and Midtjylland both need European points, making prolonged passivity difficult. Their recent records include goals scored and conceded. Opening up in search of a win could create chances at both ends. Over is my selection.", "fc-20261126-29": "CSKA Sofia vs Trabzonspor. CSKA Sofia have struggled for wins, while Trabzonspor have more victories in their official records. The hosts may prioritise rebuilding defensive organisation, and the visitors can manage the game when ahead. Discipline and tempo control support a restrained contest. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261126-30": "Borac Banja Luka vs Atalanta. Atalanta have one win in five, compared with three for Borac in the available official records. Disciplined home regrouping could force the visitors to build chances patiently. Atalanta can threaten, but home resilience and selective attacking opportunities support Borac. Borac Banja Luka is my selection.", "fc-20261126-31": "Hajduk Split vs Sint-Truidense. Hajduk have three wins in the available official five-game record. Sint-Truidense have fewer recent victories and need to improve their control of concessions. Home pressure and the use of chances provide a modest preference for Hajduk. Hajduk Split is my selection.", "fc-20261126-32": "Inter D'Escaldes vs F.C. København. Copenhagen can seek control, but Inter d’Escaldes may keep their defence compact. The hosts need to reduce the tempo rather than open the game hastily. Visiting possession and home defensive emphasis support a controlled contest. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261126-33": "KAA Gent vs Red Star Belgrade. Gent and Red Star have equal European points, but home support can help Gent apply early pressure. The visitors need disciplined recovery after losing possession. The difference is limited, with a modest preference for home control. KAA Gent is my selection.", "fc-20261126-34": "FC Nordsjælland vs Panathinaikos. Panathinaikos have five straight wins and a strong defensive record, but Nordsjaelland have scored heavily in their latest two games. Home attacking momentum can test the visitors, who also have the form to respond. Their different strengths could create opportunities at both ends. Over is my selection.", "fc-20261126-35": "SC Freiburg vs FC Twente. Freiburg have won five straight games, but Twente are also unbeaten in five. The visitors’ scoring record gives them a way to respond to home pressure. Their ability to remain competitive supports Twente in a difficult fixture. FC Twente is my selection.", "fc-20261126-36": "Braga vs KuPS Kuopio. Braga have controlled concessions in recent games and can manage the tempo. KuPS may regroup behind the ball and reduce space away from home. Home game management and visiting defensive emphasis support a more restrained scoring contest. Under is my selection.", "fc-20261127-01": "Forest are 17th on nine points, but their home win over Manchester City shows they can raise their level. Chelsea are eighth on sixteen points yet have lost their last two league matches, conceding four against Leeds. Caicedo is available again, while Forest welcome Hudson-Odoi back. Chelsea possess attacking quality, but their defensive uncertainty leaves room for the hosts to press the issue. Forest are the selection.", "fc-20261127-02": "Venezia are bottom with six points and have lost four of their last five without scoring. Their home win over Udinese offers encouragement, but Bologna bring a more sustained improvement: four wins and a draw in five, scoring in every game. Bologna are ninth with eighteen points and their varied attack can keep Venezia under pressure. Bologna are the selection.", "fc-20261127-03": "Levante have drawn their last two league games but continue to struggle for goals. Racing are seventh with seventeen points after consecutive wins over Malaga and Real Sociedad. Their defence remains vulnerable, so this is no straightforward away assignment, but their recent finishing gives them a credible route through Levante. Racing are the selection.", "fc-20261127-04": "Bremen are sixth on eighteen points after beating Hamburg without conceding. Their recent home win over Hoffenheim also shows a useful balance between attacking pressure and defensive control. Gladbach are bottom on four points and have conceded twenty-six goals in ten league games. Bremen have shown inconsistency away, but the current home attacking rhythm gives them the stronger case. Bremen are the selection.", "fc-20261127-05": "Paris FC are second on twenty-three points with four wins in five, yet Brest present a serious obstacle. The hosts are sixth on eighteen points and have won three straight league games without conceding. That organisation can deny Paris the space enjoyed in recent victories. With home advantage and a settled defensive rhythm, Brest are the selection.", "fc-20261127-06": "Middlesbrough lead the Championship with thirty-five points after consecutive wins, but Southampton remain unbeaten at St Marys. Saints are sixth on twenty-eight points after their four-point deduction and their home attack has been productive. Boro carry a genuine scoring threat, but Southampton can sustain pressure of their own. Southampton are the selection.", "fc-20261127-07": "Heidenheim are seventh on sixteen points but have failed to win in five and conceded in every game. Nuremberg are second on twenty-four points with twenty-seven league goals. Their latest defeat shows they also have vulnerabilities, yet the visitors have a stronger season-long balance and can test a fragile home defence. Nuremberg are the selection.", "fc-20261127-08": "Bochum had won three straight competitive games before losing at St Pauli, but their season total of eleven league goals limits the case for a dominant display. Darmstadt have lost only once in five and arrive after scoring three against Heidenheim. Their recent improvement gives them a route to a close contest despite a low table position. Darmstadt are the selection.", "fc-20261127-09": "Groningen have scored thirty league goals but their last five matches brought fourteen conceded. Willem II remain without a league win and have conceded forty-two in thirteen games, although they scored in their last two. Groningen can create chances, while their own defensive gaps offer the visitors opportunities. Over is the selection.", "fc-20261127-10": "Sonderjyske have conceded at least twice in each of their last four games. Brondby have failed to score in two successive defeats and need to recover their attacking rhythm. The hosts can also contribute chances, having scored twenty league goals. With both sides needing a response and defensive space likely to emerge, Over is the selection.", "fc-20261127-11": "Maritimo have failed to score in three successive competitive matches. Nacional have won two of their last three, but each of those three games was decided by a single goal. The home side need control after defensive problems, while Nacional have not shown a prolific attack. A cautious contest is plausible; Under is the selection.", "fc-20261127-12": "Leuven had gone four games unbeaten before losing at Anderlecht. Kortrijk are bottom with four points and have scored just four league goals in twelve games. The hosts also average only one league goal per game, while Kortrijk conceded only once in each of their last two defeats. The attacking limitations make Under the selection.", "fc-20261127-13": "Leganes have won three straight competitive games, scoring three in each of their last two league matches. Sabadell sit one point higher but have gone four league games without a victory and rely heavily on draws. The visitors can make this awkward, but the hosts current chance conversion and home pressure give Leganes the edge. Leganes are the selection."});
Object.assign(E.special,{"fc-20261123-02": "The key question is which relegation-threatened side can manage pressure more effectively. Monza's home advantage alone is insufficient: two wins, one draw and eight defeats from eleven games leave them eighteenth on seven points. Their convincing victory over Cagliari was followed by consecutive losses to Torino, Napoli, Bologna and Atalanta. They have struggled to protect results even when scoring, and their latest defeat brought no goal at all. Opening the game too quickly could therefore expose them again. Fiorentina's own season record is modest: two wins, three draws and six losses, nine points and fifteenth place. Their recent direction is nevertheless better. Under Vanoli they have drawn with Atalanta, won away at Sassuolo and drawn with Juventus, scoring at least twice in each of those three unbeaten games. That provides a concrete attacking route against Monza's unsettled defence. There is a counterargument: Fiorentina conceded in all five of their latest games, and the absence of Pongracic and Parisi gives the hosts opportunities. Monza's best route is to keep the contest compact and exploit mistakes rather than trade attacks. Yet their recent sequence offers little evidence that they can sustain that control, while the visitors have recovered points against difficult opposition. On current attacking output and improving results, Fiorentina are my selection.", "fc-20261120-02": "Bayern's appeal extends beyond their reputation. Six wins and three draws from nine league games, with 29 goals scored and nine conceded, show a strong balance. Three wins and a draw at home have produced 20 goals, meaning Cologne must withstand repeated pressure rather than isolated attacks. The visitors are winless in four league games and have lost all three away league fixtures this season. Bayern's absentees, including Neuer, Gnabry, Davies, Diaz and Saibari, matter, but Musiala may return and Kompany is back on the touchline. Cologne have counterattacking threats, yet defensive absences including Hubers and Van den Berg further complicate their task. Patient possession, effective counterpressing and sustained chance creation should allow Bayern to convert territorial control into a result. Bayern Munich are my special selection.", "fc-20261120-14": "Nancy's selection rests on the substance of four straight league wins, rather than second place alone. They have found ways to win different kinds of matches: beating Annecy, keeping Laval scoreless, scoring freely against Red Star and then shutting out Sochaux. Dijon deserve respect after successive league wins over Grenoble and Red Star, but earlier defeats to Reims and Rodez and a cup loss to Orleans show a less secure sequence. Nancy's own cup advancement must be described accurately: it came on penalties after a draw, not a fifth playing-time win. The hosts should protect midfield space and prevent Dijon's recent attacking improvement from turning the match into an uncontrolled exchange. With a seven-point league advantage, consistent league results and home support, Nancy have the stronger platform. Nancy are my special selection.", "fc-20261121-15": "Madrid need to maintain pressure from second place, and ten wins from twelve league games offer a stronger foundation than reputation alone. Their last five competitive matches were all victories, including meetings with Barcelona and Leipzig, with 15 goals scored and four conceded. The clean-sheet win at Valencia adds evidence of defensive control. Celta's five-goal cup win restores confidence, but their four preceding matches brought no victories and only one goal. Seven draws from twelve league matches nevertheless show that they can keep contests close. Their route to a result is to protect central space, slow Madrid's attacks and exploit impatience if the hosts do not score early. Madrid must therefore vary their tempo rather than commit too many players forward. Their recent success away from home, greater attacking production and return to home surroundings provide the stronger overall case. Real Madrid are the selection.", "fc-20261121-17": "Competition context matters here. Gladbach's victory over Standard Liege was a friendly and is excluded from their competitive form. Their official run includes wins over Stuttgart and in the cup, but a draw with Paderborn and defeat at Hamburg show that the improvement has not been sustained. One win, one draw and seven league defeats leave them bottom on four points. Dortmund are unbeaten in nine league games, with six wins and three draws for 21 points. Their last five competitive games brought four wins and a draw, including a point away at Bayern and victories over Betis and Elversberg. They are not defensively secure: six conceded in five, including one in each of the last two, give Gladbach a route into the game. The hosts can use an early goal and crowd pressure to change the contest, but their need to push forward may also create transition space. Dortmund must withstand that opening response and remain patient. Their sustained competitive record and greater ability to collect points across different match situations make Borussia Dortmund the selection.", "fc-20261116-03": "North Macedonia have reached the final group game with no points, a record exposing both their lack of cutting edge and repeated defensive lapses. A goal in Scotland offered some encouragement, but the loss continued a five-game losing streak and they have failed to score in two home outings. Slovenia's eight points are more than a statistical advantage: they earned them by restricting Switzerland to a goalless draw and winning away in Scotland. The visitors have demonstrated an ability to defend against stronger teams and stay composed away from home. Macedonia may throw players forward to rescue some pride, potentially creating spaces behind their defensive line. Slovenia should not become impatient if an early goal fails to arrive; the hosts proved in Scotland that they can still threaten on occasion. Over the full ninety minutes, the visitors' greater consistency, better defensive organisation and superior group record offer the stronger case. **Slovenia are my Special Choice.**", "fc-20261116-08": "Iceland's case rests on more than the five goals they scored away to Bulgaria. Before that emphatic result, they had beaten Luxembourg and Bulgaria without conceding and navigated a difficult trip to Estonia with a goalless draw. Those performances demonstrate the defensive control required when an opponent frustrates the attack. Iceland now lead on eleven points and have four consecutive clean sheets; Luxembourg, by contrast, have followed their opening win with four straight defeats and three consecutive games without a goal. The visitors may attempt to slow the tempo and defend deep, which would test the hosts' patience and create pressure if the score remains level. Yet Luxembourg's recent lack of attacking output makes it difficult to force Iceland into a more defensive posture. By keeping their shape and building chances methodically, the hosts should have the clearer route to success. **Iceland are my Special Choice.**", "fc-20261122-03": "Juventus need to convert their recovery into league points rather than treating this as a routine home assignment. Five wins, three draws and three defeats from eleven leave them on 18 points. Beating Napoli without conceding, winning at AZ and drawing at Fiorentina provide evidence of improvement under Spalletti, though conceding twice in Florence warns against overcommitting. Venezia gained confidence by beating Udinese, but nine league defeats and scoreless losses in their last two away games expose a weaker platform. They could frustrate Juventus by closing central spaces and slowing the contest. The decisive question is whether the hosts can maintain pressure without leaving space when possession changes. Their recent recovery, home opportunity and the visitors limited away output make Juventus the selection.", "fc-20261122-08": "Barcelona merit selection for current performance rather than reputation: eleven wins from twelve league matches and 33 points. Their victories over Alaves, Villa and Atletico demonstrate an attack capable of solving different contests. Villarreal deserve respect after beating Getafe without conceding, although their previous home league game ended in defeat to Espanyol, but the heavy European defeat to PSG exposed vulnerability when pressure intensifies. Barcelona have their own concern: Christensen is expected to miss around two games and Cubarsi needs careful management. They must protect against transitions rather than assume possession removes risk. Kounde, De Jong and Olmo being available again increases Flicks options for sustaining control and creating chances. Villarreal can make this difficult by surviving early pressure and attacking the spaces left behind. The argument for the hosts is their ability to create repeated opportunities over the full match, not an assumption of a large winning margin. With those defensive limitations acknowledged, Barcelona are the selection.", "fc-20261124-05": "Feyenoord and Porto have only three Champions League points each, so both need a win. Feyenoord have been conceding frequently, while Porto have gained confidence in attack. Both sides could open up in search of victory and have defensive weaknesses. **Over is my selection.**", "fc-20261124-12": "Charlton and Lincoln sit near the bottom of the table and have each lost four of their last five. Both struggle to finish chances and may play cautiously to avoid losing points near the relegation zone. With both attacks struggling, **Under is my selection.**", "fc-20261124-17": "Wolves sit third on 31 points and have won four and drawn one of their last five. Derby are 23rd on ten points, weak in attack and conceding frequently. Wolves' current form and home attack suggest that a wide winning margin is possible. **Wolves are my selection.**", "fc-20261125-13": "Stoke are the premium selection because the current results of both teams support the same conclusion. They are third with 32 points and ten wins in sixteen games, and have collected four wins and a draw in their last five. Beating Birmingham most recently demonstrated their ability to protect a narrow advantage against strong opposition. Victories over Preston, Blackburn and Portsmouth also show consistent conversion of opportunities. Millwall have lost three consecutive matches against QPR, West Brom and Birmingham without scoring in any of them. Their best route is to keep the defensive lines compact and make set pieces or quick breaks count. Stoke cannot afford to neglect their defensive cover or become impatient before the opening goal. Nonetheless, the home side have the stronger combination of confidence, current scoring and results. Stoke City are the selection.", "fc-20261126-02": "Home support matters, but current performance and availability are central to Celta against Bournemouth. Celta have three points from four European games; Bournemouth have won all four. In the last five official games Celta have one win, seven goals scored and seven conceded, while Bournemouth have five wins, twelve scored and two conceded. That combination shows defensive stability alongside attacking confidence. Celta confirm Borja Iglesias, Carl Starfelt and Miguel Roman are injured, requiring adjustments in both attack and defence. Space between midfield and defence after turnovers could give the visitors opportunities. Celta’s need for points and support at Balaidos provide a counterargument: early pressure could unsettle Bournemouth. The visitors therefore need to protect possession and interrupt that momentum. Marco Rose’s side have repeatedly converted patient, stable performances into victories. Combining their attacking connection, control of concessions and the hosts’ availability problems, Bournemouth are my selection.", "fc-20261127-02": "Venezia are bottom with six points and have lost four of their last five without scoring. Their home win over Udinese offers encouragement, but Bologna bring a more sustained improvement: four wins and a draw in five, scoring in every game. Bologna are ninth with eighteen points and their varied attack can keep Venezia under pressure. Bologna are the selection. Venezia have scored only eight league goals and conceded twenty-five. Bologna can recover from setbacks with a more varied attack, although their own recent clean-sheet record is imperfect. Venezia can still make home advantage count, so the visitors must keep their concentration. The current balance favours Bologna.", "fc-20261127-04": "Bremen are sixth on eighteen points after beating Hamburg without conceding. Their recent home win over Hoffenheim also shows a useful balance between attacking pressure and defensive control. Gladbach are bottom on four points and have conceded twenty-six goals in ten league games. Bremen have shown inconsistency away, but the current home attacking rhythm gives them the stronger case. Bremen are the selection. The important home pattern is not merely the latest score: Bremen combined several goals with clean sheets against Hoffenheim and Hamburg. Gladbach can defend stubbornly, as their draw with Paderborn showed, but repeated defensive pressure will test that organisation. Bremen must avoid complacency; their current home balance nevertheless makes them the premium selection."});
Object.assign(ENGLISH_NEWS,{"hot-20261120-01": ["Drone footage of Pochettino's first United training session appears online", "Drone footage of Mauricio Pochettino's first Manchester United training session appeared on YouTube on Thursday. ESPN reported that roughly 12 minutes were posted online.", "Pochettino arrived in Manchester on Wednesday after replacing Michael Carrick. The footage brought attention to external filming just as the new coaching team began work.", "The report describes Pochettino working with one group while others trained under assistant Jesus Perez. United declined to comment.", "The uploader defended the flight as compliant with regulations. That assertion does not establish club approval, and the episode may focus attention on training-ground privacy.", "United visit Liverpool at Anfield on Sunday for Pochettino's first match. The training footage should not be treated as confirmation of the starting lineup."], "hot-20261120-02": ["Juan Mata retires from playing at 38", "Juan Mata announced his retirement from professional football on November 18 at the age of 38, as reported by Reuters and Manchester United.", "The Spanish playmaker's career brought major club and international honours and lasting memories for Chelsea and United supporters.", "United highlighted his equaliser in the 2016 FA Cup final, which helped take the match into extra time before the club won the trophy.", "After leaving England, Mata played in Turkey, Japan and Australia. Retirement closes his playing career, while any future role away from the pitch remains a separate matter.", "No coaching appointment or new club position should be inferred from the retirement announcement."], "hot-20261120-03": ["Aston Villa retain Amadou Onana with a new contract", "Aston Villa announced a new contract for Amadou Onana on November 18, moving the story beyond the stage of reported negotiations.", "Retaining the Belgium midfielder gives Villa greater continuity in a central area of the team. The deal signals confidence rather than guaranteeing immediate results.", "The club also published an interview in which Onana discussed the importance of the faith shown in him.", "Attention now turns to how that stability translates into performances. The official announcement carries more weight than transfer speculation.", "Unverified salary and bonus figures are omitted. The confirmed development is that Onana has signed a new deal with Villa."], "hot-20261120-04": ["Vitor Matos takes over as Strasbourg head coach", "Strasbourg announced Vitor Matos as their new head coach on November 18, replacing Hugo Oliveira. Reuters and French outlets reported the club's confirmation.", "The move from Swansea brings a new league and a new squad for Matos to understand quickly.", "His first sessions and matches will show how much the playing style changes. The appointment itself does not confirm a particular starting formation.", "Strasbourg need to turn the new coach's ideas into performances while balancing immediate pressure with longer-term development.", "The confirmed development is the coaching appointment. Future transfers and results remain open questions."], "hot-20261120-05": ["Bay FC sign England defender Jess Carter", "Bay FC announced Jess Carter's signing on November 18 on a contract through 2028 with an option for 2029.", "The England defender arrives from Gotham with championship experience in international football, at Chelsea and in the NWSL.", "The club said Carter appeared in all 30 of Gotham's 2026 regular-season matches. Her experience at centre back and fullback offers flexibility.", "Carter said she welcomed a new challenge and wanted to earn her teammates' trust. Experience will still need to translate into a strong fit with her new side.", "With the transfer confirmed, attention turns to how Carter strengthens Bay FC's defensive organisation."], "hot-20261120-06": ["Kompany returns to Bayern touchline after treatment", "Bayern confirmed on November 19 that Vincent Kompany would return to the touchline against Cologne after missing five competitive matches while receiving medical treatment.", "The coach said he felt well again and was delighted to be back with the team. The update confirms his return to coaching duties.", "Reassembling players after international duty remains a practical challenge despite the positive results recorded during his absence.", "Bayern still have several injury absentees. Kompany said Jamal Musiala could return to the squad, which is not confirmation of a starting place.", "The Cologne match provides the first opportunity to turn the coach's return into another on-field result."], "hot-20261120-07": ["Haaland embraces greater leadership responsibility", "Erling Haaland said on November 19 that taking greater leadership responsibility at Manchester City felt natural, while stressing that he wanted to lead in his own way.", "The 26-year-old Norway striker is part of City's captaincy group this season. His comments reflect a changing role as he gains experience at the club.", "Haaland said becoming a father had also influenced his willingness to take more responsibility.", "He emphasised that new signings need time and matches to settle. That points to a role in helping the group integrate, alongside his goalscoring duties.", "Upcoming matches will show how that leadership is expressed through communication and the team's responses on the pitch."], "hot-20261120-08": ["Barco believes he can offer Chelsea more", "Valentin Barco told ESPN that he believed he could contribute much more to Chelsea and retained confidence in his ability. The interview was reported on November 19.", "The Argentina international returned to his club without appearing in his country's two latest friendlies. He said he wanted to play while still valuing national-team involvement.", "Despite limited minutes under Xabi Alonso, Barco stressed continued work and improvement rather than resignation.", "His next task is to turn that confidence into training performances and effective contributions when opportunities arrive. An interview cannot guarantee a starting place.", "The comments do not establish a transfer request or a decision to leave Chelsea."], "hot-20261120-09": ["Report: Fulham seek Bassey extension amid United interest", "Sky Sports' November 19 paper review, citing The Athletic, reported that Fulham were pushing to extend Calvin Bassey's contract.", "The report also linked the defender with Manchester United. Interest is not a confirmed bid or transfer agreement.", "A new deal could give Fulham defensive continuity and a stronger negotiating position. That is analysis of the report, not confirmation that a contract is signed.", "No verified transfer fee, salary or agreement date is available here, so none is added.", "Official confirmation from Fulham or the parties involved is still required."], "hot-20261120-10": ["Frank focuses on rebuilding Palace confidence before Coventry", "Thomas Frank is working to restore Crystal Palace's confidence before his first match against Coventry. In comments reported on November 19, he welcomed the energy in training while stressing the need for belief.", "He also joked about the coffee-cup episode from his Tottenham tenure, but Palace's on-field response remains the more important issue.", "Jean-Philippe Mateta remains suspended. Takehiro Tomiyasu is due to resume training next week, while Ismaila Sarr's return to training remains uncertain.", "Frank said he could be flexible with formations to place players in their best positions. A new appointment does not instantly establish a settled system.", "Coventry will provide the first test of whether training-ground energy becomes a stronger competitive performance."], "hot-20261121-01": ["Kane faces months out with ankle ligament injury", "Bayern confirmed on Friday that Harry Kane tore a ligament in his left ankle.", "He was injured against Cologne and examined by the club medical staff.", "The striker is expected to miss the coming months.", "Michael Olise also has a forefoot contusion and will receive treatment.", "No exact return date for Kane has been announced."], "hot-20261121-02": ["Pochettino sets out rebuilding plans at United", "Pochettino wants United to establish a new identity rather than dwell on past failures.", "His first match is at Liverpool.", "Bruno Fernandes remains central as captain.", "Restoring player confidence is a priority.", "Anfield will offer an early test of how quickly his ideas reach the pitch."], "hot-20261121-03": ["Saliba available; Zubimendi and Saka remain out", "Arteta says Saliba is available for Newcastle after recovering from his back injury.", "The defender has completed preparatory matches.", "Zubimendi faces several weeks out with a hamstring injury.", "Saka remains around four weeks away.", "Arsenal gain defensive cover but must adjust midfield and wing selection."], "hot-20261121-04": ["Maresca focuses on football as City seek a response", "Maresca rejects a link between City’s financial case and their slump.", "They face Fulham after three league defeats.", "Avoidable goals are his immediate concern.", "Marc Guehi is available again.", "The next test is restoring defensive balance without losing attacking creativity."], "hot-20261121-05": ["Christensen doubtful after new calf discomfort", "Barcelona say Christensen has discomfort in his left calf and is doubtful for Villarreal.", "The setback follows his recent return from injury.", "Recovery depends on how symptoms develop.", "Flick faces another defensive selection decision.", "Doubtful status does not yet confirm an absence."], "hot-20261121-06": ["CONMEBOL renews its backing for Infantino", "CONMEBOL’s ten associations renewed their support for Infantino on Friday.", "The endorsement followed a council meeting in Barranquilla.", "It sets out South America’s position before the March 2027 election.", "An endorsement is not an election result.", "Other associations’ responses remain relevant."], "hot-20261121-07": ["NWSL final ticket prices remain unusually high", "Resale entry prices for the Spirit–Current final have fallen from their peak.", "They remain high compared with previous NWSL finals, according to Reuters.", "Playing at Audi Field boosts local demand.", "These are changing resale prices, not a single official face value.", "The final highlights both commercial interest and affordability."], "hot-20261121-08": ["Kroupi ready to start as Scott builds minutes", "Marco Rose says Kroupi is ready to start.", "Alex Scott is also ready for increased minutes after injury.", "Rose expects Scott to start at least one of the next three matches.", "Availability does not guarantee a start against Forest.", "Managing minutes will matter during Bournemouth’s busy schedule."], "hot-20261121-09": ["Szoboszlai trains normally before United clash", "Iraola says Szoboszlai has trained normally and is fine.", "That eases concern after his knee problems on international duty.", "Van Dijk, Gravenberch and Frimpong should also be available if progress continues.", "Bradley and Leoni have resumed some training but are not ready to play.", "The final squad will clarify selection."], "hot-20261121-10": ["Nations League draw sets major quarter-final ties", "The Nations League draw on 20 November paired Spain with France.", "Norway will face England, creating a major test for Haaland’s national side.", "Belgium meet Germany and the Netherlands face Portugal.", "The official draw determines the two-legged quarter-final pairings.", "These ties will shape the route towards the finals."], "hot-20261116-01": ["Ronaldinho returns to professional football at 46 with Ravenna", "Ronaldinho's familiar smile has returned to the pitch. The Brazilian great started for Ravenna in Italy's Serie C on November 15, making a return to professional competitive football at the age of 46.", "He played the first 45 minutes of the derby against Forli. This was not merely a ceremonial exhibition appearance; he was included in Ravenna's official league starting lineup.", "His passing featured in the move that led to the opening goal. That should not be exaggerated into a personal goal or a confirmed final assist, but flashes of his technical ability were visible.", "The appearance attracted attention precisely because it came in an official competitive setting rather than a legends' friendly. Any assessment of a longer-term return should await the club's subsequent selection decisions.", "For now, the confirmed story is his first-half appearance and contribution to the build-up, not a promise that he will play every forthcoming match."], "hot-20261116-02": ["Haaland says he remains happy at Manchester City amid off-field case", "Erling Haaland has addressed questions about his future while Manchester City's off-field legal proceedings continue. Speaking after international duty, the Norway forward said he remains happy at City and focused on his football.", "Asked how possible sanctions might affect him, Haaland separated his own position from the dispute between the Premier League and the club. He said he did not know its legal details.", "His comments are not confirmation of any legal ruling. He also pointed to his long-term contract and commitment to the team rather than announcing an intention to leave.", "For City supporters, the remarks offer a clearer view of their striker's present priorities without settling the underlying proceedings.", "Any conclusion about the case or a potential transfer must be based on a separate official development, not inferred from this interview."], "hot-20261116-03": ["Klopp criticises Infantino's FIFA leadership and calls for change", "Germany coach Jurgen Klopp has criticised FIFA president Gianni Infantino's leadership. At a news conference before the Netherlands match, he expressed the view that a change at the top of world football would be appropriate.", "Klopp's central argument was that the game's interests should take precedence over financial considerations in FIFA's leadership.", "These were his opinions and criticism, not an announcement that FIFA had decided to remove its president.", "He did not confirm a replacement candidate, a resignation, or a newly concluded election outcome. Those events would require separate official confirmation.", "The comments nevertheless add a prominent coaching voice to the debate about how international football should be governed."], "hot-20261116-04": ["Maignan to undergo checks at Milan after being withdrawn against Turkey", "AC Milan are monitoring Mike Maignan's fitness after the France goalkeeper was replaced at half-time during the Nations League match against Turkey because of discomfort around his hip.", "Guillaume Restes replaced him, and the France medical staff have communicated with Milan's doctors ahead of an assessment when he returns to the club.", "The crucial uncertainty is the severity and duration of the problem. Discomfort alone does not establish a long absence, nor does it prove the issue is minor.", "Milan's immediate priority is to obtain a clear medical assessment before deciding how to manage their first-choice goalkeeper.", "An estimate of matches missed should wait for the test results and an official update. No definite recovery timetable has yet been confirmed."], "hot-20261116-05": ["Szoboszlai reveals knee concern nearly kept him out before Georgia match", "Dominik Szoboszlai played the full ninety minutes against Georgia, but admitted he had doubts about taking part before kick-off. He felt discomfort during a shooting action in the warm-up.", "The Hungary captain had been training with support around his knee. He went on to play and contributed an assist in his team's victory.", "Completing the game does not establish that the problem has disappeared. Szoboszlai said treatment would resume as he prepares for the next fixture.", "With Hungary approaching a decisive group match against Northern Ireland, the midfielder's availability matters to both his national side and Liverpool.", "Further training sessions and medical assessments should clarify whether he is ready. Claims that he is fully fit or definitely ruled out would currently go beyond the confirmed information."], "hot-20261116-06": ["Alphonso Davies set to return to Munich after Canada injury", "Bayern Munich defender Alphonso Davies is expected to return to Munich after sustaining an injury during international duty with Canada. Reports citing a Canada Soccer spokesperson say he will miss the next match against Guatemala.", "Davies slipped early in the first Guatemala game and tried to continue, before signalling to the bench that he needed to be substituted. The information confirmed so far describes a lower-body injury.", "There is concern about a possible recurrence of a muscular problem, but that possibility is not a final medical diagnosis.", "Because the full-back depends heavily on acceleration and running power, Bayern will need to manage any return carefully after evaluating him.", "No precise length of absence has been confirmed. Missing Canada's next game should not automatically be treated as confirmation that he will miss a particular number of Bayern fixtures."], "hot-20261116-07": ["Frenkie de Jong left out of Netherlands trip to Berlin as precaution", "Netherlands will be without Frenkie de Jong for their decisive meeting with Germany. The midfielder was left out of the Berlin trip as a precaution after experiencing minor discomfort following the match against Greece, according to reports citing the Dutch federation.", "De Jong had returned to international duty against Greece and even wore the captain's armband during the first half.", "Coach Xavi has opted not to call up an additional replacement. The confirmed absence concerns the Germany match; it is not evidence of a lengthy layoff at Barcelona.", "Without De Jong's ability to retain the ball and escape midfield pressure, the Netherlands must adjust their plans for a demanding away fixture.", "The matchday selection and subsequent club fitness updates will clarify the impact. The precautionary decision should not be presented as proof of a serious injury."], "hot-20261116-08": ["Mary Fowler and Kyra Cooney-Cross return to Australia's squad for Colombia friendlies", "Mary Fowler and Kyra Cooney-Cross have returned to Australia's women's national squad. They are among six recalled players in the November 16 selection for two friendlies against Colombia.", "Goalkeeper Teagan Micah also returns after missing time following a head injury. Fowler and Alanna Kennedy were among the players absent from the October international window.", "The matches are scheduled for November 28 in Canberra and December 2 in Geelong. Selection in the squad expands the coach's options but does not guarantee a starting place.", "The two fixtures are an important stage in preparations for the 2027 Women's World Cup, allowing coach Joe Montemurro to assess returning experienced players alongside current performers.", "Training progress, Micah's return and the way Fowler is integrated will be key storylines ahead of the opening game."], "hot-20261116-09": ["Andy Robertson one appearance away from moving past Kenny Dalglish", "Scotland captain Andy Robertson could make history against Switzerland. A UEFA preview published on November 15 noted that a 103rd senior international appearance would give him a new national record.", "Robertson reached 102 caps against North Macedonia, drawing level with Kenny Dalglish. Another appearance would move him clear.", "The milestone has not yet occurred simply because the next match is scheduled. He must actually take the field for cap number 103 to be confirmed.", "Sustaining a lengthy international career demands not only ability but fitness, consistency and repeated selection over many seasons.", "Scotland's team result and Robertson's personal milestone will be watched together. The official match record should be checked afterwards before reporting that the record has been broken."], "hot-20261116-10": ["Ibrahim Maza sidelined by ankle injury as Leverkusen await assessment", "Bayer Leverkusen midfielder Ibrahim Maza has suffered an ankle injury while representing Algeria. An update attributed to the Algerian football federation on November 15 confirms he will miss the next match against Togo.", "The injury occurred in the first meeting with Togo. The confirmed issue is an ankle sprain that prevents his involvement in the following international fixture.", "The available report does not set out an exact recovery period. It would therefore be premature to conclude he will definitely miss Leverkusen's next club match.", "Leverkusen will need to assess the extent of the injury and determine when the midfielder can return to training before making plans.", "His international absence is confirmed; his club availability remains dependent on further evaluation and should be reported separately."], "hot-20261122-01": ["Raya awaits scan after Arsenal injury setback", "David Raya is expected to undergo further assessment on Sunday after being forced off at Newcastle. Mikel Arteta said the precise injury was still unknown.", "The goalkeeper left holding his arm after contact with William Osula. Kepa replaced him in the 70th minute.", "The immediate concern extends beyond one result: availability of the first-choice goalkeeper affects planning for the coming fixtures.", "Neither a definite diagnosis nor a recovery period has been confirmed. Arsenal's medical update is the next development to watch."], "hot-20261122-02": ["Chelsea to reassess Caicedo after painful collision", "Xabi Alonso says Chelsea must wait for a further assessment of Moises Caicedo after his injury against Leeds. The manager described it as a knock.", "Caicedo started as captain but was replaced by Jordan Henderson after 22 minutes following a painful collision.", "Alonso felt the enforced change and subsequent equaliser disrupted Chelsea's momentum. He also said the team must respond better to setbacks.", "No absence period has been announced. The next medical assessment will determine how Chelsea prepare their midfield."], "hot-20261122-03": ["Kane begins rehabilitation after successful ankle surgery", "Bayern have confirmed that Harry Kane underwent successful surgery on his left ankle ligament injury. Rehabilitation is the next stage.", "The 33-year-old suffered the injury in the home match against Cologne. The operation is a new development following the initial injury announcement.", "Successful surgery does not establish an immediate return to playing. Bayern must plan their attack while his recovery progresses.", "The club has not provided a return date in this update. Progress through rehabilitation and training will be the next milestones."], "hot-20261122-04": ["FIFPRO criticises public pressure over Musiala contract", "FIFPRO has expressed concern about Bayern leaders publicly questioning Jamal Musiala's contract as he returns from injury.", "The union views the repeated comments as pressure on the player and his representatives before negotiations. That is its assessment, not a judicial finding.", "FIFPRO says uncertainty can add mental strain during recovery and argues that contractual concerns should be discussed privately.", "No contract change is confirmed by the statement. Bayern's response and subsequent discussions remain the next developments."], "hot-20261122-05": ["Rafael Nadal elected to Real Madrid board", "Real Madrid say Rafael Nadal was elected to their board with 99.5 per cent support at the extraordinary general assembly on November 21.", "The honorary club member was welcomed by delegates and said he wanted to learn and contribute in his new responsibility.", "This is an institutional appointment rather than a playing or coaching role. His wider sporting experience adds a new perspective to the board.", "Detailed responsibilities should not be assumed beyond the announcement. The club's subsequent governance work will show how the role develops."], "hot-20261122-06": ["Perez reaffirms member ownership at Real Madrid", "Florentino Perez has told Real Madrid's general assembly that the club is not for sale and will continue to belong to its members.", "The president said members would decide the institution's future while distinguishing new revenue projects from a transfer of ownership.", "Plans for direct fan relationships and digital experiences form part of the wider commercial discussion. Proposals should be distinguished from adopted rules.", "The speech does not announce a sale. Further structural proposals and any member decisions are the developments to monitor."], "hot-20261122-07": ["Flick confirms Christensen absence and careful squad management", "Hansi Flick expects Andreas Christensen to miss around two matches, while Pau Cubarsi needs careful monitoring before Villarreal.", "Kounde, Frenkie de Jong and Dani Olmo are available again, increasing the coach's options despite defensive limitations.", "Nine matches in 27 days make workload management a wider issue than one lineup. Flick emphasised balancing playing time.", "Christensen's absence and Cubarsi's condition should not be treated as identical. The squad list and further medical updates will clarify availability."], "hot-20261122-08": ["Ekitike remains on January return plan", "Andoni Iraola says Hugo Ekitike remains on course for a January return after the Achilles injury he suffered in April.", "An earlier return would require exceptionally good progress; the current plan has not changed. He remains behind Bradley and Leoni in rehabilitation.", "The update does not mean he is ready for immediate selection. Recovery still has to progress through the necessary training stages.", "January remains the target rather than a guaranteed appearance date. Club confirmation of team training and match readiness will be the next milestones."], "hot-20261122-09": ["Werder extend Thioune deal before northern derby", "Werder have extended Daniel Thioune's contract ahead of the northern derby with Hamburg. The announcement came on November 21.", "Appointed in February, he helped secure survival and has taken the team to sixth after nine matches this season.", "Assistants Jan Hoepner and Christian Gross have also extended their agreements, supporting continuity across the coaching staff.", "The new term has not been disclosed. Progress over the season, rather than one derby result, will show how the renewed backing develops."], "hot-20261122-10": ["Bompastor urges patience over Ramirez recovery", "Sonia Bompastor says Mayra Ramirez remains in rehabilitation and has not yet rejoined team training. Being seen with the squad does not establish match readiness.", "After a lengthy absence following hamstring surgery, the forward needs time to rebuild. Chelsea will continue assessing her during the international break.", "Manaka Matsukubo was available on the Liverpool bench but was not used after glute pain. Squad inclusion and full fitness are different stages.", "Bompastor expects a clearer Ramirez update after the break. No precise return to starting action has been confirmed for either player."], "hot-20261123-01": ["Doue to undergo surgery after knee ligament injury", "PSG confirmed on 22 November that Desire Doue ruptured the anterior cruciate ligament in his right knee and will undergo surgery after being injured against Nice.", "He could not continue after injuring the knee while protecting the ball and left on a stretcher. Luis Enrique expressed concern after the match before the diagnosis was confirmed.", "The absence requires another redistribution of attacking responsibilities. The coaching staff must assess how to replace his contribution and adjust the attack.", "PSG have not announced an official return date. Estimates of a lengthy absence should remain distinguished from a confirmed club timetable; surgery and rehabilitation updates are the next developments."], "hot-20261123-02": ["Villarreal reject eclipse claim about Pepe eye surgery", "Villarreal denied on 22 November that Nicolas Pepe needed eye surgery because he viewed a solar eclipse. The club says the procedure and that event were unrelated.", "Pepe missed matches in October following surgery. Reports later linked his absence to social-media footage, prompting the club to respond.", "The club says the operation was planned beforehand for unrelated medical reasons and called for accurate, responsible reporting about player health.", "The confirmed development is the official rejection of the circulating explanation. Further medical details should not be inferred beyond the statement."], "hot-20261123-03": ["Fernandes puts contract talks on hold to prioritise United recovery", "Bruno Fernandes said in an interview published on 22 November that United offered a new contract, but discussions are on hold while he prioritises the team returning to winning ways.", "He confirmed talks took place at the end of last season and the beginning of this one. He believes the current context makes this the wrong moment to continue negotiations.", "He rejected the suggestion that demands for more money or years explain the pause. His comments do not constitute an announcement that he will leave.", "United must manage their captain's future alongside the recovery of the team. A resumption of negotiations or an agreement would be the next material development."], "hot-20261123-04": ["Watford part company with Alessio Dionisi", "Watford announced on 22 November that Alessio Dionisi had left his role as head coach after the heavy defeat at Sheffield United.", "Sporting director Luke Dowling thanked Dionisi and his staff for their professionalism and efforts, and said the search for a replacement had begun.", "The change comes during a busy fixture period, leaving limited training time for a successor. Restoring results and stability will be immediate priorities.", "The departure and replacement process are confirmed; a new appointment requires a separate announcement. Reported candidates should not be treated as appointed."], "hot-20261123-05": ["Boxall future unresolved as Minnesota contract talks continue", "Minnesota United confirmed that Michael Boxall's contract expired but negotiations over a new deal continue. His future remained unresolved in the 23 November report.", "The New Zealand defender has been with the club since 2017. Injury management and reduced playing time affected the latter part of his season.", "Local reporting describes a gap in salary expectations, but the club has not announced that negotiations have failed. Boxall has previously expressed a wish to stay.", "An expired contract does not establish a completed move elsewhere. A Minnesota agreement or another confirmed destination remains the next development."], "hot-20261123-06": ["Bell calls 36 players for Myanmar women friendlies", "ASEAN Football Federation reported on 22 November that Myanmar women's coach Colin Bell called 36 players for two friendlies against Hong Kong.", "The matches are scheduled for 1 and 4 December at Thuwanna Stadium in Yangon during the international window.", "The group offers the coaching staff options to assess players and combinations across two fixtures. A call-up does not mean every player will start.", "The final match squads and Bell's selections are the next sporting developments. Kick-off, ticket and access information should follow separate official announcements."], "hot-20261123-07": ["Williamson reaches 300-appearance Arsenal milestone", "Leah Williamson reached the 300-appearance milestone for Arsenal Women when named in the starting side against West Ham on 22 November. Official team news and club congratulations recognised the landmark.", "The long-serving defender represents experience and leadership. The milestone reflects sustained service rather than a single season's form.", "Renee Slegers praised Williamson's deep connection to Arsenal and commitment in the matchday programme, congratulating her career and wishing for more to come.", "Alongside the celebration, Arsenal must continue pursuing their current objectives. How they use her experience within the present squad remains relevant."], "hot-20261123-08": ["Report links Antonee Robinson with Manchester United interest", "A 22 November transfer report, citing Football Insider, links Fulham left-back Antonee Robinson with Manchester United interest. This remains a media report, not an agreement confirmed by either club.", "The report connects him to a stated January priority at left-back. Robinson previously played under Mauricio Pochettino for the United States.", "Previous working familiarity may matter, but it does not establish that a transfer will happen. Fulham's position and any actual bid are more material.", "No fee, medical or contract terms can be presented as confirmed on this basis. An official announcement or substantiated bid would represent a further development."], "hot-20261123-09": ["Lavia calls for a Chelsea response without panic", "Romeo Lavia said on 22 November that Chelsea must respond to disappointment without panic following their home defeat to Leeds.", "He acknowledged anger within the squad and failure to meet the home supporters' expectations, while maintaining confidence in the team.", "His central message was to turn the pain of defeat into a response in the next match, analyse the problems and improve.", "The comments do not prove the problems are resolved. Fewer mistakes and greater stability in subsequent performances will test that response."], "hot-20261123-10": ["Pochettino disputes Yoro red card as VAR upholds decision", "Mauricio Pochettino disputed Leny Yoro's dismissal after the Liverpool match on 22 November, questioning whether Alexander Isak could retain control of the ball.", "Yoro was sent off outside the penalty area for denying an obvious goalscoring opportunity. VAR checked and upheld the original decision.", "Pochettino and Kobbie Mainoo argued that the ball was already heading towards the goalkeeper. Those comments represent United's view, not a reversal of the decision.", "The defensive selection and disciplinary implications remain relevant. Any appeal or successful overturning requires a separate official confirmation."], "hot-20261125-01": ["Madrid overturn deficit to beat PSV 5-1", "Real Madrid recovered from a half-time deficit to defeat PSV 5-1. Valverde and Bellingham turned the match, Mbappe scored twice and Vinicius added the fifth. Madrid have fifteen points from five Champions League games."], "hot-20261125-02": ["City twice recover to draw with Napoli", "Manchester City and Napoli drew 2-2. Hojlund and Noa Lang put Napoli ahead on separate occasions, with Bouaddi and Cherki equalising. Allegri described the point as important despite regret over the late equaliser."], "hot-20261125-03": ["Arsenal held by Dortmund after Beier equaliser", "Arsenal led through Gyokeres but drew 1-1 with Dortmund after Beier's second-half equaliser. Missed opportunities prevented the hosts from securing all three points; Dortmund leave with a valuable away result."], "hot-20261125-04": ["Liverpool train in Brugge before European test", "Liverpool completed their pre-match workout at Jan Breydel Stadium after travelling from Merseyside.", "Andoni Iraola's squad prepare for their fifth league-phase match against Club Brugge. Training participation does not confirm the starting line-up."], "hot-20261125-05": ["Barcelona travel to Baku without Yamal", "Lamine Yamal stayed in Barcelona with an ankle issue as the squad travelled to Baku.", "Rodri, Xavi Espart and Christensen are also absent through injury. Flick retains senior options including Pedri, Raphinha and De Jong for an important European away match."], "hot-20261125-06": ["Inter and Stuttgart set for first competitive meeting", "Inter's official guide confirms that this will be the clubs' first competitive meeting; four previous encounters were friendlies.", "Inter have won their last two European games, while Stuttgart lost at Galatasaray. A one-point gap gives the match immediate standings significance."], "hot-20261125-07": ["Bayern must adapt in Lille without Kane", "Bayern face Lille without Harry Kane after an ankle ligament injury against Cologne, according to the Bundesliga's match build-up.", "The visitors remain unbeaten in four European games but need wins to improve their position. The attack must distribute his finishing responsibility."], "hot-20261125-08": ["Galatasaray edge Aston Villa in Istanbul", "Galatasaray beat Aston Villa 1-0 in their Champions League home match. Protecting the narrow lead and keeping a clean sheet secured three points, while Villa were unable to find an equaliser."], "hot-20261125-09": ["Porto secure narrow away victory at Feyenoord", "Porto won 1-0 at Feyenoord, protecting their advantage until full time. The visitors take three important Champions League points, while Feyenoord missed the opportunity to capitalise on home advantage."], "hot-20261125-10": ["Lola Brown: Chelsea's young talent and her love of art", "Chelsea have profiled nineteen-year-old Lola Brown after her impressive display in the draw with Liverpool.", "She discussed painting, decorating boots for supporters and looking up to Virgil van Dijk and Lucy Bronze. The feature offers context beyond her football performances."], "hot-20261126-01": ["Pochettino sees aggression developing but disputes key decisions", "Mauricio Pochettino praised United’s aggressive approach after a 2-2 draw at Sporting but felt key decisions had hurt his side.", "The club’s official reaction presents the performance as an early sign of his intended style, even though a first victory remains elusive.", "His criticism is an attributed opinion, rather than an official finding that the referee made errors.", "United still need to turn promising phases into secure results, with concentration in decisive moments central to that task.", "Upcoming matches will show whether their more assertive approach can produce greater consistency."], "hot-20261126-02": ["Bayern and Musiala’s representatives put health first", "Bayern announced constructive talks with Jamal Musiala’s management on 25 November, stressing that the player’s health comes first.", "The statement follows speculation about his condition and contract. Both sides intend to continue discussions cooperatively and privately.", "They clarified that his first examination for absence-like neurological symptoms took place in April 2025. This history does not establish a return date.", "Bayern must plan the sporting side while respecting verified medical information.", "Further official updates, rather than speculation, will determine the next stage of his recovery."], "hot-20261126-03": ["Iraola praises Isak’s link play as attacking partnership develops", "Andoni Iraola praised Alexander Isak’s contribution beyond his two goals against Club Brugge.", "The striker provided an outlet against aggressive pressing, helping Liverpool connect their play in the first half.", "Iraola explained that a deeper second-half approach left space to exploit when the hosts committed players forward.", "He linked the improving Isak–Wirtz partnership to better collective performances rather than individual form alone.", "That understanding could strengthen Liverpool’s attacking options through a crowded schedule."], "hot-20261126-04": ["Frank updates Sarr and Tomiyasu; Mateta available in Europe", "Thomas Frank discussed Palace’s unavailable players ahead of Real Sociedad.", "Takehiro Tomiyasu is moving closer to team training after a calf problem, while Ismaila Sarr’s groin issue still affects his return.", "Jean-Philippe Mateta can play because his three-match suspension applies to domestic fixtures.", "Frank emphasised balancing freshness with a consistent team rhythm during a long season.", "His first European home match brings squad management and the Selhurst Park atmosphere into focus."], "hot-20261126-05": ["Amorim demands European consistency from Milan", "Ruben Amorim says Milan must perform in Europe as well as Serie A to develop into a strong side.", "He does not attribute their European defeats simply to rotation and wants the approach shown in stronger domestic performances.", "Improvement in the final third and a defence that has conceded frequently remain priorities.", "Ardon Jashari also spoke about staying ready and increasing his contribution when selected.", "Olympiacos’ intense home environment will test whether Milan can translate those principles into a European performance."], "hot-20261126-06": ["Celta name 24-man squad with three confirmed injury absences", "Celta announced a 24-player squad for Bournemouth on 25 November.", "Claudio Giraldez can call on Iago Aspas, Pablo Duran and Williot Swedberg among his attacking options.", "The club confirmed that Borja Iglesias, Carl Starfelt and Miguel Roman are unavailable through injury.", "Those absences require adjustments in both attack and defence as Celta seek to use home advantage.", "The official starting line-up will clarify the final combinations and defensive structure."], "hot-20261126-07": ["Hinds looks to inspire the next generation before Ukraine play-off", "Taylor Hinds spoke on 25 November as England prepare for their Women’s World Cup qualifying play-off against Ukraine.", "The Lionesses are at St George’s Park before the first leg in Spain on 1 December and the Wembley return on 5 December.", "The successful UK bid for the 2035 Women’s World Cup provides an encouraging backdrop.", "Hinds pointed to the impact of EURO 2022 and hopes another major home tournament can inspire children to play.", "The immediate sporting objective remains qualification for the 2027 World Cup through the two-legged tie."], "hot-20261126-08": ["Yoro’s domestic suspension removed after successful appeal", "The FA removed Leny Yoro’s one-match suspension after United successfully appealed his dismissal against Liverpool.", "The decision announced on 24 November concerns wrongful dismissal; it does not alter the match result.", "Yoro is therefore available for United’s next domestic league fixture, restoring a defensive option.", "An on-field decision and a subsequent disciplinary appeal are separate processes.", "United must now turn the additional availability into a more stable defensive unit."], "hot-20261126-09": ["Fermín López receives two-match domestic ban", "Fermín López was handed a two-match suspension on 25 November following his Villarreal dismissal.", "The Spanish federation’s disciplinary decision rules him out of league games against Deportivo La Coruña and Atlético Madrid.", "He was dismissed for protesting to the fourth official from the bench. The sanction affects domestic selection.", "Barcelona lose an attacking midfield option during a demanding run of fixtures.", "The Atlético match makes replacement roles particularly relevant; any further official decision will need to be checked."], "hot-20261126-10": ["Burnley’s home league winless run reaches 24 matches", "ESPN reported that Burnley reached a 24-match home league winless run after losing to Birmingham on 25 November.", "The Turf Moor result highlights a sustained problem rather than a single disappointing evening.", "The reported record concerns league matches, not every friendly and cup fixture.", "Such a prolonged sequence increases pressure and makes rebuilding confidence an important part of the response.", "Burnley’s next home league fixture offers another opportunity to end the run and recover valuable points."], "hot-20261127-01": ["Dominic Calvert-Lewin commits to Leeds until 2029", "Leeds confirmed on 26 November that Dominic Calvert-Lewin has signed a two-and-a-half-year contract running until summer 2029.", "The striker scored fifteen goals in all competitions last season, helping Daniel Farkes side retain Premier League status.", "His influence also extends to creating chances. He scored against Chelsea and helped set up Noah Okafor in that victory.", "The extension gives Leeds continuity in attack. Maintaining his scoring and link play will be the next test."], "hot-20261127-02": ["Alonso says Fofana interview dispute is closed", "Xabi Alonso said on 26 November that Wesley Fofana had apologised following an unauthorised interview and that the matter was closed.", "The episode drew attention at a time when Chelsea need to improve their league results. Alonso is seeking to return the focus to football.", "The confirmed development is the apology and the managers response. Details of any internal sanction have not been established here.", "Chelsea next need an on-field response at Nottingham Forest, particularly through a more organised defensive performance."], "hot-20261127-03": ["FIFA confirms cyberattack involving personal and business data", "FIFA confirmed on 26 November that a criminal cyberattack resulted in unauthorised access to some personal and business information.", "The organisation described the affected set as limited. Further official detail will matter when assessing the incident.", "FIFA condemned unlawful acquisition and publication of information. Private details are not needed to explain the public significance of the breach.", "The next issue is how the organisation addresses the incident and communicates confirmed findings, without treating speculation as fact."], "hot-20261127-04": ["Fabregas keeps his immediate focus on Como", "Cesc Fabregas played down Barcelona links in reports on 26 November and said his immediate priority remains Como.", "His history with Barcelona explains the questions, but an emotional connection and a current coaching commitment are different matters.", "No completed agreement to coach Barcelona is established by these comments. His stated focus is continuing to develop in his present role.", "For Como, the practical issue is continuity in preparation and performance in the next matches."], "hot-20261127-05": ["Bruno Fernandes leaves open a future Sporting return", "Bruno Fernandes said he would not rule out a future return to Sporting, according to reporting on 26 November.", "The midfielder retains a connection with the Portuguese club, which he left for Manchester United.", "Openness to a future return is not confirmation of a transfer or a signed agreement. That distinction remains essential.", "His current contribution to United and any subsequent confirmed decision are more meaningful than assuming an immediate move."], "hot-20261127-06": ["Kimmich criticises public handling of Musiala situation", "Joshua Kimmich criticised Bayerns public handling of Jamal Musialas situation in reports on 26 November.", "He defended his teammates effort and objected to the way the matter had been discussed publicly. This is a new player response to an existing issue.", "The comments raise questions about communication and trust. They do not establish any transfer decision.", "Bayerns next response and how the parties communicate will be the developments to follow."], "hot-20261127-07": ["Lewis-Potter signs Brentford contract until 2032", "Brentford confirmed on 25 November that Keane Lewis-Potter has signed until summer 2032, with an option for a further year.", "The twenty-five-year-old has started all eleven league games this season, scoring four times and providing one assist.", "Keith Andrews highlighted his development, versatility and consistency, explaining the long-term football case for the deal.", "The extension preserves an established part of the squad. Maintaining that consistency is the next task."], "hot-20261127-08": ["Brighton confirm six-to-ten-week absence for Yalcouye", "Fabian Hurzeler confirmed on 25 November that Malick Yalcouye faces an absence of six to ten weeks.", "Brighton said the midfielder would miss their next three Conference League league-phase matches, affecting European as well as domestic planning.", "The club are exploring a replacement in the European squad. No completed replacement has been confirmed in this report.", "The immediate task is managing the available squad. A precise return date awaits further club updates."], "hot-20261127-09": ["Caicedo available for Forest as two Chelsea absences continue", "Xabi Alonso confirmed on 26 November that Moises Caicedo is available to face Nottingham Forest after coming off against Leeds.", "The midfielder has trained, but Joao Pedro and Maxence Lacroix remain unavailable for the match.", "Caicedos return increases Chelseas options for ball recovery and protecting the defence as they seek better results.", "Availability is not confirmation of a starting place. The final midfield selection and its defensive balance remain to be seen."], "hot-20261127-10": ["Hayes expects major El Salvador test with World Cup place at stake", "Emma Hayes said on 26 November that the United States expect a major challenge from El Salvador with a World Cup place at stake.", "The teams meet in the Concacaf W Championship quarterfinal in Mansfield, Texas. Victory secures qualification for the 2027 Womens World Cup.", "Hayes expects maximum commitment from El Salvador. Reputation alone cannot replace concentration and execution on the field.", "The key questions are how the United States use their early pressure and manage any response in a decisive qualifying match."]});
